(function(){
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const E=(w,origin)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/'+w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')});
const Q=(id,senseId,errorType,prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain)=>({id,senseId,type:'辨義與用法',errorType,prompt,options:[answer,d1,d2],answer,explain});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistakes,quiz)=>D(w,{etymology:E(w,origin),contexts,mistakes,quiz});
P('usage','From Old French usage, “custom or practice,” based on user, “to use.”',[C('usage.s1','语言规范','The handbook explains British usage of the present perfect with recent events.','手冊說明英式英語在談及近期事件時如何使用現在完成式。','usage of + word / construction','Noun: the way a word or expression is normally used in a language.','It describes a language convention, not an individual action.'),C('usage.s2','使用方式','The usage of water in the factory fell after the cooling system was replaced.','更換冷卻系統後，工廠的用水量下降了。','usage of + resource','Noun: the act of using something, or the amount used.','The figure measures consumption of water.')],[M('The usage guide says “fewer” is used with count nouns, but it is a book describing language customs only by measuring gallons.','The usage guide explains the customary use of “fewer” with count nouns.','A language usage guide describes word use, not a physical quantity.')],[Q('usage.q1','usage.s1','meaning','What does the handbook explain about the present perfect?','Its customary use in British English.','How many litres a factory consumes.','How to repair a cooling system.','Usage can mean the normal way language is used.'),Q('usage.q2','usage.s2','context','Why did factory usage fall?','The plant consumed less water after replacing its system.','The handbook changed a grammar rule.','The factory produced fewer dictionaries.','This sense refers to consumption or amount used.'),Q('usage.q3','usage.s1','distinction','Which book focuses on word usage?','A guide showing when speakers say “who” or “whom.”','A meter recording household electricity use.','A report listing water consumption.','The guide explains language conventions.'),Q('usage.q4','usage.s2','word-choice','Which phrase refers to resource consumption?','daily usage of electricity','usage of the subjunctive in formal writing','usage notes on a dictionary entry','The first measures how much electricity is used.')]);
P('use','From Old French user, from Latin uti, “employ or make use of.”',[C('use.s1','工具或方法','Use the insulated gloves to lift the hot tray from the oven.','請戴上隔熱手套，將熱烤盤從烤箱中取出。','use + tool / method + to-infinitive','Transitive verb: employ an object or method to do something.','The gloves are the means for lifting the tray.'),C('use.s2','利用或消耗','The company used temporary workers during the harvest and used up its extra budget.','公司在收成期間雇用了臨時工，也花光了額外預算。','use a person / resource','Verb: take advantage of someone or consume a supply.','The example includes employing workers and consuming money.'),C('use.s3','用途或使用','The room has many uses, but its main use is storing medical records.','這個房間有多種用途，主要用來存放醫療紀錄。','the use of + noun; have a use','Noun: the purpose of something or the act of using it.','The room’s purpose is record storage.'),C('use.s4','好处','One use of the spare key is that a neighbour can enter during an emergency.','備用鑰匙的一項好處是緊急時鄰居可以進屋。','a use / benefit of + thing','Noun: a benefit or advantage.','The key offers a practical benefit.')],[M('Use the insulated gloves to lift the tray, but hold the hot metal with your bare hands.','Use the insulated gloves to lift the tray rather than touching the hot metal with bare hands.','The incorrect instruction defeats the protective purpose of using heat-resistant gloves.','context')],[Q('use.q1','use.s1','context','What should protect your hands while lifting the hot tray?','Insulated gloves.','A wet paper napkin.','Bare hands.','The gloves are a tool used to lift hot cookware safely.'),Q('use.q2','use.s2','meaning','What did the company do with its extra budget?','It consumed the budget during the harvest.','It stored the budget in a room.','It used the money to make a dictionary.','Use can mean consume a supply.'),Q('use.q3','use.s3','distinction','What is the main use of the room?','Storing medical records.','Giving neighbours a spare key.','Employing temporary workers.','Here use names the room’s purpose.'),Q('use.q4','use.s4','word-choice','Which is a benefit of keeping a spare key?','A neighbour can enter during an emergency.','It records the grammar of a sentence.','It consumes the household electricity.','The advantage of the key is emergency access.')]);
P('use up','Phrasal verb formed from use + up, with up marking exhaustion of the whole supply.',[C('use up.s1','用完物资','The crew used up all the clean water before the rescue boat reached the island.','救援船抵達島上前，船員已用完所有乾淨飲水。','use up + supply / money / time','Phrasal verb: consume all of a supply.','No clean water remains.'),C('use up.s2','耗尽精力','The long rehearsal used up the actors’ patience before the director finished giving notes.','漫長排練在導演講完意見前就耗盡了演員的耐心。','use up someone’s energy / patience','Phrasal verb: exhaust the energy or patience available.','The rehearsal leaves the actors with none of the resource.')],[M('The crew used up all the water but still had every full tank untouched for the return trip.','The crew saved some water because the tanks remained full for the return trip.','If every tank is still full, the water has not all been used up.')],[Q('use up.q1','use up.s1','meaning','What happened to the clean water?','The crew consumed all of it.','The crew saved every tank untouched.','The rescue boat brought a new supply.','Use up means consume the whole supply.'),Q('use up.q2','use up.s2','context','Why were the actors impatient?','The rehearsal exhausted their patience.','They had not started rehearsing.','They had extra water to drink.','The phrasal verb can mean exhaust a person’s patience.'),Q('use up.q3','use up.s1','distinction','Which household action uses up a supply?','Burning the last of the heating oil.','Refilling the oil tank.','Putting a full oil can in storage.','The last of the supply is consumed.'),Q('use up.q4','use up.s2','word-choice','Which event could use up your energy?','Climbing a steep trail all afternoon.','Taking a short rest in a chair.','Filling a bottle with fresh water.','A demanding climb can exhaust available energy.')]);
P('useable','From use + -able, with an extra e retained before the suffix; it is a spelling variant of usable.',[C('useable.s1','可使用','The storm-damaged tent is still useable if the owner replaces its torn groundsheet.','只要更換破損的地布，這頂暴風雨後受損的帳篷仍可使用。','useable for + purpose','Adjective: able to be used; the spelling with e is a variant of usable.','The tent can serve its purpose after a repair.')],[M('The tent was useable because it had no poles, no fabric, and could not shelter anyone.','The tent was unusable because it had no poles, no fabric, and could not shelter anyone.','An item that cannot serve its purpose is unusable, not useable.','word-choice')],[Q('useable.q1','useable.s1','meaning','Why is the tent still useable?','It can shelter someone after its groundsheet is replaced.','It has no fabric or poles.','It cannot be repaired.','Useable means capable of being used.'),Q('useable.q2','useable.s1','spelling','Which statement about useable is accurate?','It is a spelling variant of usable.','It means impossible to use.','It is the past tense of use.','The source accepts useable with an e as a variant spelling.'),Q('useable.q3','useable.s1','context','Which item is useable after a simple repair?','A chair with one loose screw that can be tightened.','A chair reduced to splinters.','A broken chair thrown away and missing every leg.','The repair restores the chair’s function.'),Q('useable.q4','useable.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate sentence.','The map is useable after the missing corner is copied from a spare.','The map is useable although every mark has vanished.','The map is useable because nobody can read it.','It remains capable of guiding someone after repair.')]);
P('used','Past participle of use; as an adjective it means accustomed to something or not new.',[C('used.s1','习惯于','After years in the desert, the botanist was used to working in extreme heat.','在沙漠多年後，植物學家已習慣在酷熱中工作。','be used to + noun / gerund','Adjective: familiar with a situation so it no longer seems strange.','Repeated experience makes the heat familiar.'),C('used.s2','二手','They bought a used microscope from a university that had upgraded its laboratory.','他們從一所已升級實驗室的大學買了一台二手顯微鏡。','used + object for sale','Adjective: not new; previously owned or operated.','The microscope had an earlier owner.')],[M('She bought a used bicycle that had never belonged to anyone and was brand new in its original box.','She bought a new bicycle that had never belonged to anyone and was brand new in its original box.','An item never owned and brand new is new, not used.')],[Q('used.q1','used.s1','meaning','What does “used to working in extreme heat” mean?','The botanist is accustomed to it.','The botanist is using heat as a tool.','The botanist has never experienced heat.','Be used to means familiar through experience.'),Q('used.q2','used.s2','context','Why was the microscope used?','A university owned it before selling it.','It had just left the factory for the first time.','It could not magnify anything.','Used as an adjective means not new.'),Q('used.q3','used.s1','grammar','Which phrase means “accustomed to”?','She is used to long shifts.','She used to long shifts yesterday.','She is used a long shift.','Be used to takes a noun or gerund for familiarity.'),Q('used.q4','used.s2','distinction','Which is a used item?','A secondhand desk bought from its former owner.','A desk bought new from the maker.','A desk that has not yet been manufactured.','The former owner has already used the desk.')]);
P('used to','Fixed past construction from use + infinitive marker to; it describes a former habit or state that has changed.',[C('used to.s1','过去习惯','Before the railway opened, villagers used to walk two hours to reach the market.','鐵路開通前，村民過去常走兩小時去市場。','used to + base verb','Semi-modal construction: a repeated past action that no longer happens.','The habit belonged to the past.'),C('used to.s2','熟悉','I am used to the morning noise from the bakery across the street.','我已經習慣街對面麵包店早晨的噪音。','be used to + noun / gerund','Adjective phrase: familiar through repeated experience.','The noise no longer feels strange.')],[M('Before the railway opened, villagers used to walk two hours every day, and they still make the same walk now.','Before the railway opened, villagers used to walk two hours every day, but they no longer do.','Used to describes a past habit that no longer continues.')],[Q('used to.q1','used to.s1','meaning','What did villagers used to do before the railway opened?','Walk two hours to the market as a past habit.','Ride the new railway every morning.','Live beside the market.','Used to + base verb describes a repeated past action.'),Q('used to.q2','used to.s2','context','What does the speaker mean by “I am used to the noise”?','The morning noise feels familiar now.','The bakery has never made noise.','The speaker used the noise as a tool.','Be used to means accustomed to something.'),Q('used to.q3','used to.s1','grammar','Choose the correct past-habit form.','They used to walk to the market.','They are used to walk to the market.','They used walking to the market yesterday.','The past-habit construction is used to + base verb.'),Q('used to.q4','used to.s2','distinction','Which phrase expresses familiarity rather than a former habit?','She is used to working nights.','She used to work nights but now works days.','They used to travel by train.','Be used to + gerund means accustomed to the activity.')]);
P('useful','From use + -ful, “full of use”; it can mean practical, helpful, or worth the effort.',[C('useful.s1','实用','A small torch is useful when the power fails during a storm.','暴風雨停電時，小手電筒很實用。','useful for + purpose','Adjective: works well and saves effort for a practical task.','The torch helps people see in darkness.'),C('useful.s2','有帮助','The nurse gave useful advice about caring for the child’s fever at home.','護理師提供了有幫助的建議，說明如何在家照顧發燒的孩子。','useful advice / information to someone','Adjective: providing help or benefit in a situation.','The advice assists the family.'),C('useful.s3','值得花时间','The short course was useful because it taught the mechanic to read the new diagnostic codes.','這門短期課程很值得，因為它教會技師解讀新的診斷代碼。','useful to do / for + goal','Adjective: worth the time and effort spent.','The course produces a practical skill.')],[M('The torch was useful in the blackout because it produced no light and made the room harder to see.','The torch was useless in the blackout because it produced no light and made the room harder to see.','A light that produces no light cannot help in a blackout.')],[Q('useful.q1','useful.s1','meaning','Why was the torch useful during the outage?','It helped people see in the dark.','It produced no light.','It repaired the power line.','A practical tool helps with the task.'),Q('useful.q2','useful.s2','context','How did the nurse’s advice help the family?','It explained how to care for the child’s fever.','It increased the child’s fever.','It replaced the thermometer with a torch.','Useful advice provides help in a situation.'),Q('useful.q3','useful.s3','distinction','Why was the course useful to the mechanic?','It taught a skill needed to read diagnostic codes.','It took time but taught nothing relevant.','It explained how to use a torch at home.','The course was worth the effort because it gave a practical skill.'),Q('useful.q4','useful.s1','word-choice','Choose the phrase about a practical tool.','a useful torch during a blackout','useful advice from a nurse','a useful course for learning diagnostic codes','The torch directly serves a practical purpose.')]);
P('usefully','From useful + -ly, an adverb meaning so as to produce a practical benefit.',[C('usefully.s1','实用地','The guide usefully groups the emergency numbers by service, so readers can find the right one quickly.','指南將緊急電話依服務分類，讓讀者能快速找到所需號碼，十分實用。','usefully + explain / organize / provide','Adverb: in a way that gives a practical benefit.','The arrangement saves readers time.')],[M('The guide was usefully organized, but it buried every emergency number in an unlabeled paragraph.','The guide was poorly organized because it buried every emergency number in an unlabeled paragraph.','Hiding key numbers makes the guide less useful, not usefully organized.','word-choice')],[Q('usefully.q1','usefully.s1','meaning','How did the guide help readers?','It grouped emergency numbers so people could find one quickly.','It removed every phone number.','It mixed all numbers in an unlabeled paragraph.','Usefully means in a way that gives practical benefit.'),Q('usefully.q2','usefully.s1','context','Which note is usefully placed?','A warning appears beside the control it explains.','A warning is hidden in an unrelated appendix.','A label is printed on the back of an inaccessible cabinet.','The warning is positioned to help the user act.'),Q('usefully.q3','usefully.s1','grammar','What does usefully modify in “The chart usefully separates the results”?','The way the chart separates the results.','The results as a noun.','The chart’s paper size.','The -ly adverb modifies separates.'),Q('usefully.q4','usefully.s1','distinction','Which organization is usefully arranged?','Tools are grouped by task for quick selection.','Tools are scattered randomly across a dark room.','Tools are listed without names or labels.','Grouping by task makes selection easier.')]);
P('usefulness','From useful + -ness, the quality of being useful or serving a purpose.',[C('usefulness.s1','实用价值','The trial measured the usefulness of the warning label by checking whether workers noticed it.','試驗透過檢查工人是否注意到警告標籤，衡量它的實用價值。','the usefulness of + tool / information','Noun: the quality of helping people or serving a purpose.','The study tests whether the label actually helps.')],[M('The label’s usefulness was proven by the fact that it gave workers no information and prevented no mistakes.','The label’s uselessness was shown by the fact that it gave workers no information and prevented no mistakes.','A label that gives no help has little usefulness; the evidence points to uselessness.')],[Q('usefulness.q1','usefulness.s1','meaning','What did the trial measure?','Whether the warning label helped workers notice danger.','How expensive the factory was.','How many colours appeared on the label.','Usefulness is the quality of serving a helpful purpose.'),Q('usefulness.q2','usefulness.s1','context','What would demonstrate a map’s usefulness?','Hikers use it to find a safe route.','The map is unreadable and leads nowhere.','The paper is stored but never consulted.','A map is useful when it helps with navigation.'),Q('usefulness.q3','usefulness.s1','distinction','Which question concerns usefulness?','Does this checklist prevent missed safety steps?','What colour is the checklist cover?','Who printed the checklist?','The first asks whether it serves a practical purpose.'),Q('usefulness.q4','usefulness.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','test the usefulness of the new search tool','test the useful of the new search tool','test the usefully of the new search tool','Usefulness is the noun naming the quality of being useful.')]);
P('useless','From use + -less, “without use”; it can mean ineffective for a purpose or very poor at a task.',[C('useless.s1','无效','The key was useless because it did not fit any lock in the building.','這把鑰匙對大樓裡的任何門鎖都不合用，因此毫無用處。','useless for / in + task','Adjective: unable to achieve what is needed.','The key cannot open the intended locks.'),C('useless.s2','不擅长','I am useless at remembering names, so I write them down after each meeting.','我很不擅長記人名，所以每次會議後都把名字寫下來。','useless at + noun / gerund','Adjective: very bad at doing something, or of very low quality.','The speaker has poor ability at this task.')],[M('The key was useless because it opened every lock in the building on the first try.','The key was useful because it opened every lock in the building on the first try.','A key that opens all the locks works well and is useful.')],[Q('useless.q1','useless.s1','meaning','Why was the key useless?','It did not fit any lock it was meant to open.','It opened every lock immediately.','It was made for the building’s doors.','Useless means unable to achieve the intended result.'),Q('useless.q2','useless.s2','context','What does the speaker mean by “useless at remembering names”?','The speaker is very bad at remembering names.','The speaker has no names to remember.','Names cannot be written down.','This construction describes poor ability at a task.'),Q('useless.q3','useless.s1','distinction','Which tool is useless for cutting metal?','A blunt plastic spoon.','A sharp steel saw.','A powered cutter designed for steel.','The spoon cannot do the intended job.'),Q('useless.q4','useless.s2','grammar','Choose the natural pattern.','She is useless at keeping track of receipts.','She is useless to keeping track of receipts.','She useless at keeps track of receipts.','Useless at is followed by a noun or gerund.')]);
P('user','From use + -er, an agent noun for a person, organization, or machine that uses something.',[C('user.s1','产品或服务使用者','Each user of the water service receives a monthly notice before the meter is read.','水務服務的每位使用者都會在抄表前收到月度通知。','a user of + product / service','Noun: a person, organization, or machine that uses a product or service.','The person receives the utility service.'),C('user.s2','账户使用者','The application asks each user to create a password before opening an account.','應用程式要求每位使用者先建立密碼，才能開設帳戶。','computer / app user; user account','Noun: someone who operates a computer system or application, especially with an account.','The person logs into the application.')],[M('Each user of the application was locked out, but the sentence says every person successfully signed in and used the account.','Each user of the application was logged in, but the sentence says every person successfully signed in and used the account.','A person who successfully signs in is a logged-in user, not locked out.')],[Q('user.q1','user.s1','meaning','Who receives the water-service notice?','Each person or organization using the service.','Only the person who repairs the meter.','Anyone who never receives water.','User can name someone who uses a service.'),Q('user.q2','user.s2','context','Why does the application ask a user to create a password?','To let the person open and access an account.','To measure the water meter.','To operate a theatre entrance.','An app user operates the system through an account.'),Q('user.q3','user.s1','distinction','Which is a user of a machine?','A laboratory technician operating the microscope.','A visitor who has never touched or accessed it.','A repair manual stored beside it.','The technician operates the equipment.'),Q('user.q4','user.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase tied to a computer account.','a registered application user','a user of the municipal water supply','a user of a kitchen utensil','The registered app user operates the application through an account.')]);
P('usher','From Old French ussier, “doorkeeper,” from Latin ostiarius, “porter”; it is a verb and a person noun.',[C('usher.s1','引领入场','A volunteer ushered the guests into the hall before the award ceremony began.','頒獎典禮開始前，志工引領賓客進入大廳。','usher someone into / to + place','Transitive verb: lead or guide someone in.','The volunteer guides guests to their seats.'),C('usher.s1','接待人员','The usher showed the couple to their seats near the front of the theatre.','引座員帶那對夫婦到劇院前方的座位。','an usher at a theatre / wedding','Noun: an attendant who guides guests at a theatre, wedding, or court.','The worker directs the couple to their seats.')],[M('The usher showed guests to their seats by locking the doors and refusing to let anyone enter.','The usher admitted the guests and guided them to their seats.','An usher guides people in; barring entry contradicts that role.','context')],[Q('usher.q1','usher.s1','meaning','What did the volunteer do?','Guided the guests into the hall.','Sold the guests theatre tickets.','Locked the doors before anyone arrived.','The verb means lead someone into a place.'),Q('usher.q2','usher.s1','context','Who showed the couple to their theatre seats?','An attendant who guides guests.','A ticket printer.','A stage actor.','An usher is the theatre attendant who directs guests.'),Q('usher.q3','usher.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses usher as a verb?','The guard ushered visitors through the side entrance.','The usher wore a blue uniform.','An usher waited beside the auditorium door.','In the first, ushered means guided visitors in.'),Q('usher.q4','usher.s1','word-choice','Choose the person noun use.','The wedding usher guided relatives to their places.','The ushered guests entered the hall.','The host ushered relatives inside.','Here usher names the attendant.')]);
P('using','From use + -ing, the gerund or participle describing employment of a tool, skill, or resource.',[C('using.s1','使用工具或资源','Using a calibrated scale, the technician measured the powder before mixing the solution.','技師使用校準過的秤，在混合溶液前先量取粉末。','using + tool / skill / resource + to do','Gerund or participle: employing something to accomplish an action.','The scale is the instrument used for weighing.')],[M('Using the calibrated scale, the technician measured nothing and left the powder unweighed.','Using the calibrated scale, the technician measured the powder before mixing it.','If the technician uses the scale to measure, the powder is weighed.')],[Q('using.q1','using.s1','meaning','What did the technician use to measure the powder?','A calibrated scale.','A theatre ticket.','An empty mixing bowl only.','Using means employing a tool for a task.'),Q('using.q2','using.s1','context','Which sentence shows using a skill?','Using her sign-language skills, Mei helped the visitor communicate.','Mei ignored the visitor and left the room.','The visitor bought a calibrated scale.','Her skill is employed to help communication.'),Q('using.q3','using.s1','grammar','What does the opening phrase “Using a scale” tell us?','The instrument the technician employed.','The result of the mixture.','The scale’s manufacturing date.','The participial phrase identifies the tool used.'),Q('using.q4','using.s1','distinction','Which action is using a resource?','The crew burns stored fuel to power the generator.','The crew stores new fuel without touching it.','The crew measures a theatre seat.','They employ and consume the fuel for a purpose.')]);
P('usual','From Old French usuel, from Latin usualis, “customary,” based on usus, “use or custom.”',[C('usual.s1','通常情况','The usual bus arrives at the village stop just after seven each weekday.','平日裡，通常那班公車會在七點剛過抵達村站。','the usual + noun; as usual','Adjective: normal because it happens most of the time.','The bus follows its recurring pattern.'),C('usual.s2','平常不特别','For a usual lunch, the crew ate soup and bread in the workshop.','工作人員照平常一樣在工坊裡吃湯和麵包當午餐。','usual routine / place / way','Adjective: ordinary, not special or different.','The lunch is ordinary for this group.')],[M('The usual bus arrived at a never-used stop on a route it had never travelled before.','An unusual bus arrived at a stop on a route it had never travelled before.','A first-time route is not the normal recurring bus service.')],[Q('usual.q1','usual.s1','meaning','When does the usual bus arrive?','Just after seven on weekdays.','Only once every ten years.','At a different time each day with no pattern.','Usual means normal because it happens most of the time.'),Q('usual.q2','usual.s2','context','What did the crew eat for a usual lunch?','Their ordinary soup and bread meal.','A special feast served only once.','A bus schedule.','The meal is not special or different from their routine.'),Q('usual.q3','usual.s1','distinction','Which event is usual?','The clinic opens at the same hour every weekday.','The clinic opens at midnight for the first time.','The clinic closes forever.','The recurring schedule is normal.'),Q('usual.q4','usual.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase about something ordinary.','her usual seat beside the window','an extraordinary seat reserved for the mayor','a newly installed seat used for the first time','The first is her ordinary, customary place.')]);
P('usually','From usual + -ly, an adverb meaning on most occasions or in most cases.',[C('usually.s1','频率','The ferry usually leaves before sunset unless strong winds delay the crossing.','除非強風耽誤航程，渡輪通常會在日落前出發。','usually + verb; usually, + clause','Adverb of frequency: on most occasions, though not necessarily every time.','The departure is the common pattern with exceptions.')],[M('The ferry usually leaves before sunset, but it has never once left before sunset in its entire history.','The ferry rarely leaves before sunset, although it has done so on some occasions.','Usually indicates the common pattern; never once contradicts the stated regularity.')],[Q('usually.q1','usually.s1','meaning','How often does the ferry leave before sunset?','On most occasions, except when winds delay it.','Never, under any circumstances.','Only once in its history.','Usually expresses a pattern that occurs more often than not.'),Q('usually.q2','usually.s1','context','Which statement uses usually correctly?','The clinic usually closes at six, though it stays open late on Fridays.','The clinic usually closed once in 1992.','The clinic always closes at six with no exceptions.','Usually allows a common pattern with exceptions.'),Q('usually.q3','usually.s1','grammar','Where does usually naturally appear?','The ferry usually leaves before sunset.','The usually ferry leaves before sunset.','The ferry leaves before usually sunset.','The adverb typically comes before the main verb.'),Q('usually.q4','usually.s1','distinction','What does usually mean here?','More often than not.','Every single time with no exception.','Only in the distant past.','The ferry has a common, but not absolute, schedule.')]);
P('ute','Ethnonym for the Ute people of the Great Basin; the deeper derivation is uncertain.',[C('ute.s1','族群','The Ute people have lived in the Great Basin region of the western United States for generations.','Ute族世世代代生活在美國西部的大盆地地區。','the Ute people / a Ute community','Proper noun: a member of an Indigenous people of the Great Basin.','The word names a people, not a vehicle or utensil.')],[M('The Ute are an Indigenous people of the Great Basin, but the report calls them a brand of kitchen appliance.','The Ute are an Indigenous people of the Great Basin, not a brand of kitchen appliance.','Ute names a people; it must not be confused with unrelated abbreviations or products.','meaning')],[Q('ute.q1','ute.s1','meaning','Which people does Ute name in this entry?','An Indigenous people of the Great Basin.','A group of kitchen appliances.','A type of bus.','The dictionary sense identifies the Ute people of the western United States.'),Q('ute.q2','ute.s1','context','Where is the Great Basin mentioned in the context?','As the region where the Ute people have lived for generations.','As a vehicle manufacturing centre.','As a room for cooking utensils.','The term is an ethnonym connected with that region.'),Q('ute.q3','ute.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses Ute as the people’s name?','Ute community in the Great Basin','a utility vehicle called a ute','a kitchen utensil made of steel','The assigned lexical sense refers to the Indigenous people.'),Q('ute.q4','ute.s1','word-choice','Choose the respectful, source-aligned sentence.','The Ute people are Indigenous to the Great Basin region.','The Ute are a cooking tool.','The Ute people are a bus model.','The word names the Indigenous people, not objects.')]);
P('utensil','From Latin utensilia, “things for use,” via French; it names a household or kitchen tool or container.',[C('utensil.s1','厨房器具','Use a clean utensil to transfer the cooked rice into the serving bowl.','請用乾淨的器具把煮好的米飯盛進餐碗。','a kitchen / cooking / serving utensil','Noun: a tool or hollow container used to prepare, cook, or serve food.','The implement transfers food hygienically.')],[M('Use a clean utensil to transfer the rice, then stir it with your bare shoe.','Use a clean utensil to transfer and stir the rice.','A shoe is not a kitchen utensil and is not a hygienic food tool.','word-choice')],[Q('utensil.q1','utensil.s1','meaning','What is the clean utensil used for?','Moving cooked rice into a serving bowl.','Measuring the bus route.','Storing a whole dinner table.','A utensil is a tool used in preparing or serving food.'),Q('utensil.q2','utensil.s1','context','Which item is a kitchen utensil?','A ladle used to serve soup.','A bus pass.','A garden fence.','A ladle is a food-serving implement.'),Q('utensil.q3','utensil.s1','distinction','Which utensil is hollow and used to serve?','A small serving bowl.','A door hinge.','A paper timetable.','The source includes hollow containers used in the kitchen.'),Q('utensil.q4','utensil.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','a cooking utensil for stirring soup','a cooking utensil for measuring a valley','a cooking utensil worn as underwear','Utensils are household tools for food preparation or serving.')]);
P('utensils','Plural of utensil, from Latin utensilia, “things for use”; it refers collectively to kitchen tools and containers.',[C('utensils.s1','厨房器具集合','The drawer holds utensils for peeling vegetables, mixing batter, and serving dinner.','抽屜裡放著削蔬菜、攪麵糊和上菜用的各種廚房器具。','kitchen / cooking / serving utensils','Plural noun: a collection of hollow tools and containers used to prepare, cook, or serve food.','Several implements serve different kitchen tasks.')],[M('The drawer of utensils contained only one knife, although the sentence describes a collection of tools and containers.','The drawer of utensil contained only one knife.','The plural utensils refers to a collection; the singular form would be utensil.')],[Q('utensils.q1','utensils.s1','meaning','What does the drawer contain?','A collection of tools for several food tasks.','A single bus ticket.','Only a tablecloth.','Utensils is plural and names kitchen implements collectively.'),Q('utensils.q2','utensils.s1','context','Which group counts as utensils?','A peeler, mixing spoon, and serving tongs.','A map, bus pass, and umbrella.','A table, chair, and window.','These are tools for preparing or serving food.'),Q('utensils.q3','utensils.s1','grammar','Choose the plural form.','The utensils are in the drawer.','The utensils is in the drawer.','The utensil are in the drawer.','Utensils is plural, so it takes are.'),Q('utensils.q4','utensils.s1','distinction','Why is “utensils” plural in the example?','It refers to several kitchen implements together.','It is the name of one hollow cup.','It is the verb for cooking.','The plural form describes a collection.')]);
P('utilisation','From utilise + -ation, the British spelling of utilization; it names making practical use of something.',[C('utilisation.s1','资源使用','The report assessed the utilisation of rainwater across the school’s buildings.','報告評估了全校各棟建築的雨水利用情況。','utilisation of + resource / capacity','Noun: the act of making practical use of a resource.','The study considers how the rainwater resource is put to use.')],[M('The report measured rainwater utilisation, but every collected litre was discarded without being used.','The report measured rainwater waste, because every collected litre was discarded without being used.','Discarding all collected water is waste, not utilisation.')],[Q('utilisation.q1','utilisation.s1','meaning','What did the report assess?','How the school made practical use of rainwater.','How many windows each building has.','How the rainwater was discarded unused.','Utilisation names the act of using a resource.'),Q('utilisation.q2','utilisation.s1','spelling','Which spelling is the British form?','utilisation','utilizashun','utilization is the only British form','The -isation spelling is the British variant.'),Q('utilisation.q3','utilisation.s1','context','Which study concerns utilisation?','A study of how a hospital uses its available beds.','A study counting beds that are locked away and never used.','A study of the hospital’s painted walls.','The first measures practical use of capacity.'),Q('utilisation.q4','utilisation.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','better utilisation of stored energy','utilisation of energy that is thrown away unused','utilisation to describe a room’s wall colour','Utilisation concerns putting resources to practical use.')]);
P('utilitarian','From utility + -arian, ultimately from Latin utilis, “useful”; it can describe practicality or the ethical doctrine.',[C('utilitarian.s1','实用主义设计','The cabin has utilitarian furniture: sturdy chairs and shelves, with little decoration.','小屋的家具以實用為主：椅子和架子堅固，裝飾不多。','utilitarian design / object / purpose','Adjective: designed for practical use rather than appearance.' ,'The furniture prioritizes function.'),C('utilitarian.s1','伦理学','A utilitarian argument supports the policy if it increases overall welfare.','功利主義論證會在政策提高整體福祉時支持它。','utilitarian ethics / argument','Adjective: related to the ethical view that actions are right when they produce the greatest good.','The judgment depends on consequences for overall welfare.')],[M('The cabin chose utilitarian furniture for its elaborate decoration and lack of any practical function.','The cabin chose ornamental furniture for its elaborate decoration and lack of any practical function.','Elaborate decoration without practical function is ornamental, not utilitarian.')],[Q('utilitarian.q1','utilitarian.s1','meaning','Why was the cabin furniture utilitarian?','It was sturdy and chosen for practical function.','It was selected only for elaborate decoration.','It could not be used for sitting or storage.','The design sense prioritizes practical use.'),Q('utilitarian.q2','utilitarian.s1','context','What does the utilitarian argument weigh?','Whether the policy increases overall welfare.','Whether the policy uses attractive chairs.','Whether the policy is old-fashioned.','The ethical sense judges consequences for overall good.'),Q('utilitarian.q3','utilitarian.s1','distinction','Which room is furnished utilitarianly?','A workshop with durable benches arranged for work.','A gallery with fragile objects displayed only for beauty.','A room with no furniture or function.','The workshop prioritizes practical function.'),Q('utilitarian.q4','utilitarian.s1','word-choice','Choose the ethical use of utilitarian.','A utilitarian may defend a choice by its benefit to the whole community.','A utilitarian chair is simply made of wood.','A utilitarian curtain matches the wall.','The ethical doctrine weighs the overall consequences.')]);
P('utilitarianism','From utilitarian + -ism, the ethical doctrine associated with judging actions by their effects on overall welfare.',[C('utilitarianism.s1','伦理学','Utilitarianism would compare the likely benefits and harms of each plan for everyone affected.','功利主義會比較每個方案對所有受影響者可能造成的利弊。','utilitarianism judges actions by consequences','Noun: an ethical doctrine that judges acts by their consequences for overall welfare.','The decision is assessed by its effects on the whole community.')],[M('Utilitarianism judges the policy only by whether its author intended well, regardless of its effects on anyone.','Utilitarianism judges the policy by its consequences for overall welfare.','The doctrine evaluates consequences and overall welfare, not intention alone.')],[Q('utilitarianism.q1','utilitarianism.s1','meaning','What does utilitarianism compare in the example?','The likely benefits and harms for everyone affected.','Only the author’s private intention.','Which plan has the nicest name.','The doctrine judges actions by their effects on overall welfare.'),Q('utilitarianism.q2','utilitarianism.s1','context','Which question is utilitarian?','Which choice will improve welfare for the greatest number?','Which choice will look most traditional?','Which choice rewards only its proposer?','The ethical test concerns consequences for the group.'),Q('utilitarianism.q3','utilitarianism.s1','distinction','What would a utilitarian argument consider?','The outcomes of a policy for all affected people.','Only whether the policy is old.','The colour of the printed policy.','Consequences are central to utilitarianism.'),Q('utilitarianism.q4','utilitarianism.s1','word-choice','Choose the sentence using utilitarianism correctly.','The council used utilitarianism to weigh public benefits against harms.','The council used utilitarianism to describe a chair’s wood.','The council used utilitarianism to mean a city power bill.','The term names an ethical doctrine about overall welfare.')]);
P('utility','From Old French utilite, from Latin utilitas, “usefulness”; it has public-service and practical-use senses.',[C('utility.s1','公共服务','The storm damaged a utility line, leaving the village without electricity.','暴風雨損壞了公用事業管線，讓村莊停電。','a utility company / line / bill','Noun: a public service such as water, gas, or electricity.','The damaged line carries electricity to homes.'),C('utility.s2','实用性','The utility of the checklist became clear when it prevented a missed safety step.','清單避免漏掉安全步驟後，它的實用價值便顯而易見。','the utility of + tool / information','Noun: the quality of being useful.' ,'The checklist serves a practical purpose.'),C('utility.s3','实用型','They bought a utility knife with a replaceable blade for workshop jobs.','他們買了一把可換刀片的多用途刀，供工坊工作使用。','utility + vehicle / knife / clothing','Adjective: designed to be useful rather than decorative.','The knife is chosen for function.')],[M('The storm damaged a utility line, but the line was a decorative ribbon with no public service.','The storm damaged a decorative ribbon, but it carried no public service.','A utility line carries a public service such as electricity, not decoration.','word-choice')],[Q('utility.q1','utility.s1','meaning','What kind of line did the storm damage?','A public-service line carrying electricity.','A decorative ribbon.','A private hiking trail.','A utility can be a public service like electricity.'),Q('utility.q2','utility.s2','context','How did the checklist show its utility?','It prevented a missed safety step.','It decorated the workshop wall.','It used up the power supply.','Its practical usefulness became clear.'),Q('utility.q3','utility.s3','distinction','Why is the knife called a utility knife?','It is designed for practical workshop tasks.','It is valued only for its decoration.','It supplies gas to the workshop.','Utility as an adjective emphasizes practical function.'),Q('utility.q4','utility.s1','word-choice','Which bill is a utility bill?','A household electricity bill.','A bill for a theatre costume.','A receipt for a decorative painting.','Electricity is a public utility service.')]);
P('utilization','From utilize + -ation, the American spelling of utilisation; it means making use of a resource or capacity.',[C('utilization.s1','资源使用','The study tracked utilization of the clinic’s evening appointments after the hours were extended.','診所延長晚間門診後，研究追蹤了時段的使用情況。','utilization of + resource / capacity','Noun: making use of a resource, capacity, or service.','The study measures whether patients use the extra slots.')],[M('The clinic’s appointment utilization was high, although every evening slot remained empty.','The clinic’s appointment utilization was low, because every evening slot remained empty.','Empty appointment slots indicate low, not high, utilization.')],[Q('utilization.q1','utilization.s1','meaning','What did the study track?','How patients used the clinic’s extended evening slots.','How many doctors had a holiday.','The clinic’s wall decorations.','Utilization measures use of available capacity.'),Q('utilization.q2','utilization.s1','spelling','Which is the American spelling of this noun?','utilization','utilisation only','utilizashun','The -ization spelling is the American variant.'),Q('utilization.q3','utilization.s1','context','Which statistic measures utilization?','The percentage of available lab machines currently in use.','The number of machines painted blue.','The number of machines stored unused forever.','It measures how much of a resource is being used.'),Q('utilization.q4','utilization.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses utilization naturally?','utilization of the new training service','decoration of the training room','ownership of the training building','The noun refers to making use of the service.')]);
P('utilize','From utility, via French utilité and Latin utilis, “useful”; the verb means employ something or make good use of it.',[C('utilize.s1','使用资源','The farmers utilize rainwater to irrigate the vegetable plots during dry weeks.','乾旱週期間，農民利用雨水灌溉菜畦。','utilize + resource / tool + for purpose','Transitive verb: use something for a practical purpose.','Rainwater is employed for irrigation.'),C('utilize.s2','善用机会','The designer utilized the narrow space beneath the stairs as a storage cupboard.','設計師善用樓梯下方的狹窄空間，改成儲物櫃。','utilize a skill / space / opportunity','Transitive verb: make good use of a skill, space, or chance.','The awkward area is put to effective use.')],[M('The farmers utilized the rainwater for irrigation by leaving every tank sealed and sending no water to the fields.','The farmers stored the rainwater instead of utilizing it for irrigation.','Water left sealed and unused has not been utilized.')],[Q('utilize.q1','utilize.s1','meaning','How did the farmers utilize rainwater?','They used it to irrigate their crops.','They left it sealed in every tank.','They used it to build a cupboard.','Utilize means put a resource to practical use.'),Q('utilize.q2','utilize.s2','context','What did the designer do with the space under the stairs?','Made good use of it as a cupboard.','Closed it off without using it.','Turned it into a water source.','The space was used efficiently.'),Q('utilize.q3','utilize.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses utilize for a resource?','The lab utilizes recycled glass in its experiments.','The lab has a useful storage cupboard.','The lab’s utility bill arrived today.','Recycled glass is employed for a practical purpose.'),Q('utilize.q4','utilize.s2','word-choice','Choose the example of utilizing a skill.','Mina used her translation training to help the visiting team.','Mina ignored her language skills during the meeting.','Mina bought a new dictionary and left it unopened.','She makes effective use of a learned skill.')]);
P('utmost','From Old English ūtmest, a superlative form meaning outermost or greatest; now used for maximum degree or effort.',[C('utmost.s1','最大程度','The laboratory handled the rare sample with the utmost care.','實驗室以極度謹慎的態度處理這份稀有樣本。','the utmost + care / importance / caution','Adjective: greatest in degree.','The care is as great as possible.'),C('utmost.s2','最大努力','The crew did its utmost to keep the clinic open during the storm.','暴風雨期間，工作人員盡最大努力維持診所開放。','do one’s utmost; to the utmost','Noun: the greatest effort or furthest limit.','The crew makes its maximum effort.')],[M('The crew did its utmost to keep the clinic open by making no effort and abandoning the building.','The crew made little effort to keep the clinic open and abandoned the building.','Abandoning the work is not doing one’s utmost.')],[Q('utmost.q1','utmost.s1','meaning','How carefully did the laboratory handle the sample?','With the greatest possible care.','With no caution at all.','Only after throwing it away.','Utmost means greatest in degree.'),Q('utmost.q2','utmost.s2','context','What did the crew do to keep the clinic open?','Made the greatest effort it could.','Abandoned the building without trying.','Reduced the clinic’s opening hours before the storm.','Do one’s utmost means make one’s maximum effort.'),Q('utmost.q3','utmost.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses utmost for degree?','the utmost importance','the utmost effort made by the crew','an outermost wall','The first describes importance at the greatest degree.'),Q('utmost.q4','utmost.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase meaning “try as hard as possible.”','do your utmost','do the usual','reach an ordinary level','Do your utmost means make your greatest effort.')]);
P('utopia','Coined by Thomas More from Greek ou-topos, “no place,” for an imagined ideal society.',[C('utopia.s1','理想社会','The novel imagines a utopia with fair laws, secure housing, and equal access to education.','小說描繪了一個法律公平、住房穩定、教育機會平等的理想社會。','imagine / create / seek a utopia','Noun: an imagined society with ideal laws, government, and living conditions.','The society is presented as nearly perfect.'),C('utopia.s2','完美处境','After weeks at sea, the quiet island seemed a utopia to the exhausted crew.','在海上航行數週後，這座寧靜島嶼對疲憊的船員而言彷彿是無憂樂土。','seem / feel like a utopia','Noun: a place or situation that appears free from trouble and unhappiness.','The island feels free of the crew’s hardships.')],[M('The novel’s utopia is a society where injustice and hunger are worse than anywhere else.','The novel’s dystopia is a society where injustice and hunger are worse than anywhere else.','A society dominated by injustice and hunger is dystopian, not utopian.')],[Q('utopia.q1','utopia.s1','meaning','What kind of society does the novel imagine?','A society with ideal laws and living conditions.','A place defined by worsening injustice and hunger.','A real city with no laws.','A utopia is an imagined ideal society.'),Q('utopia.q2','utopia.s2','context','Why did the island seem like a utopia to the crew?','It felt peaceful after weeks of hardship at sea.','It had more storms than the ocean.','It was a difficult government system.','The place seemed free from their troubles.'),Q('utopia.q3','utopia.s1','distinction','Which work describes a utopia?','A story about a society with fair laws and education for all.','A story about a collapsed state ruled by fear.','A travel log listing real bus timetables.','The ideal society is the defining feature.'),Q('utopia.q4','utopia.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','The quiet garden felt like a utopia after the noisy city.','The novel designed a perfect government for its utopia.','The island’s laws formed an imagined utopia.','The garden is described as a trouble-free situation.')]);
P('utopian','From utopia + -an, describing an idealized perfect society or an idea unlikely to work in practice.',[C('utopian.s1','不切实际的理想','The plan for free transport, housing, and meals for everyone sounded utopian without a funding source.','在沒有資金來源的情況下，免費提供所有人交通、住房和餐食的計畫聽來過於理想化。','utopian plan / vision / ideal','Adjective: based on the idea that society can be perfect, but unlikely to be achieved in practice.','The proposal assumes an ideal outcome without practical means.')],[M('The utopian plan was already funded, tested, and operating successfully in every district.','The practical plan was already funded, tested, and operating successfully in every district.','A functioning, funded program is not merely an unattainable ideal.')],[Q('utopian.q1','utopian.s1','meaning','Why did the plan sound utopian?','It promised ideal services but had no realistic funding source.','It had been tested and funded in every district.','It concerned only a bus timetable.','Utopian can describe a perfect but impractical social vision.'),Q('utopian.q2','utopian.s1','context','Which proposal is utopian?','A promise to end every social problem overnight without a plan.','A funded program already operating successfully.','A modest change tested in one school.','The first imagines perfection without a practical route.'),Q('utopian.q3','utopian.s1','distinction','What criticism does utopian often imply?','The ideal may be impossible to achieve in practice.','The idea is already proven and ordinary.','The idea is too small to matter.','Utopian ideals can be impractical.'),Q('utopian.q4','utopian.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','Critics called the unfunded promise of universal free housing utopian.','The completed low-cost repair was utopian because it was routine.','The bus arrived on time, a utopian timetable.','The promise aims at an ideal with no practical funding plan.')]);
P('utter','From Old English ūtor, “outer”; as a verb it means speak, and as an adjective it intensifies “complete.”',[C('utter.s1','说出声音','The witness could barely utter a word after seeing the damaged bridge.','目擊者看到受損的橋後，幾乎說不出一句話。','utter a word / sound / cry','Transitive verb: say a word or make a sound with the voice.','The witness struggles to speak.'),C('utter.s2','完全','The engine stopped in utter silence when its last warning light went dark.','最後一盞警示燈熄滅時，引擎完全靜了下來。','utter + negative noun (nonsense, failure, silence)','Adjective: complete, used to strengthen a negative noun.','Silence is total.')],[M('The witness uttered silence by writing three pages of spoken testimony aloud.','The witness uttered a word by speaking one brief sentence.','Utter as a verb means say or make a sound, not “utter silence.”','word-choice')],[Q('utter.q1','utter.s1','meaning','What could the witness barely do?','Say a word aloud.','Make the engine completely silent.','Repair the bridge.','The verb utter means speak or make a sound.'),Q('utter.q2','utter.s2','context','What does utter add to “silence”?','It makes the silence complete or total.','It means someone spoke loudly.','It names a witness’s sentence.','The adjective intensifies the negative noun.'),Q('utter.q3','utter.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses utter as a verb?','She uttered a quiet warning.','The room fell into utter darkness.','It was utter nonsense.','The first describes speaking a sound.'),Q('utter.q4','utter.s2','word-choice','Choose the adjective use.','The claim was utter nonsense.','He uttered a single syllable.','She uttered the name carefully.','Utter strengthens nonsense to mean complete nonsense.')]);
P('utterance','From utter + -ance, a noun for something spoken or the manner of speaking.',[C('utterance.s1','说出的内容','The child’s first clear utterance was the name of her older brother.','孩子第一句清楚說出的話是哥哥的名字。','an utterance of + word / statement','Noun: a spoken word or statement.','The name is something she says aloud.'),C('utterance.s2','表达方式','The actor’s slow, deliberate utterance made each warning sound serious.','演員緩慢而清晰的表達方式讓每句警告聽起來都很嚴肅。','the manner / clarity of an utterance','Noun: the way words are spoken or expressed.','The focus is on delivery rather than exact words.')],[M('Her utterance was a spoken statement, but she never said or expressed anything aloud.','Her utterance was a spoken statement that she expressed aloud.','An utterance is something spoken, so it must be expressed aloud.')],[Q('utterance.q1','utterance.s1','meaning','What was the child’s first clear utterance?','Her brother’s name, spoken aloud.','The way an actor moved on stage.','A silent written note.','An utterance can be a spoken word.'),Q('utterance.q2','utterance.s2','context','Why did the actor’s utterance sound serious?','The words were delivered slowly and deliberately.','The actor did not speak at all.','The written script used a large font.','This sense concerns how speech is expressed.'),Q('utterance.q3','utterance.s1','distinction','Which is an utterance as spoken content?','“Wait here,” said aloud by the guard.','The guard’s clear pronunciation style.','The guard’s silent gesture.','The quoted instruction is a spoken statement.'),Q('utterance.q4','utterance.s2','word-choice','Which phrase describes the manner of speaking?','the measured utterance of each line','the exact utterance “good morning”','a short utterance from the child','Measured describes the delivery or expression.')]);
P('utterly','From utter + -ly, an adverb meaning completely or used to strengthen a judgment or feeling.',[C('utterly.s1','完全地','The old pump was utterly unusable after its motor flooded.','舊水泵的馬達進水後完全無法使用。','utterly + adjective','Adverb: to the fullest extent, with nothing left out.','The pump cannot be used at all.'),C('utterly.s2','加强负面评价','I was utterly exhausted after carrying the equipment up six flights of stairs.','把器材搬上六層樓後，我累壞了。','utterly + negative adjective / judgment','Adverb: intensifies a judgment or feeling, often a negative one.','The adverb strengthens the speaker’s exhaustion.')],[M('The pump was utterly usable because it could not work at all after its motor flooded.','The pump was utterly unusable because it could not work at all after its motor flooded.','A machine that cannot work is unusable, not usable.')],[Q('utterly.q1','utterly.s1','meaning','How usable was the flooded pump?','It could not be used at all.','It worked perfectly.','It needed only a new label.','Utterly means completely or to the fullest extent.'),Q('utterly.q2','utterly.s2','context','How tired was the speaker after carrying the equipment?','Completely exhausted.','Slightly hungry but energetic.','Not tired at all.','Utterly intensifies the feeling of exhaustion.'),Q('utterly.q3','utterly.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses utterly to mean completely?','utterly impossible to repair','utterly tired after climbing','utterly angry at the delay','Impossible is total in degree.'),Q('utterly.q4','utterly.s2','word-choice','Choose the intensifier use.','The reviewer called the argument utterly absurd.','The engine was utterly without fuel.','The machine was utterly unusable.','The adverb strengthens the negative judgment absurd.')]);
P('vacancy','From Latin vacantia, “emptiness,” from vacare, “be empty”; it can be a job opening or a free hotel room.',[C('vacancy.s1','职位空缺','The hospital advertised a vacancy for a night pharmacist.','醫院刊登了一個夜班藥師的職缺。','a vacancy for + job; fill a vacancy','Noun: a job that is open because no one is doing it.','No pharmacist currently holds the post.'),C('vacancy.s2','空房','The receptionist checked for a vacancy before directing the tired driver to the hotel.','接待員先查詢是否有空房，再引導疲憊的駕駛到旅館。','a room vacancy; no vacancies','Noun: a hotel room that is free for a guest.','A room is available to be occupied.')],[M('The hotel had a vacancy, but every room was occupied and no guest could stay.','The hotel had no vacancy because every room was occupied.','An occupied hotel with no available room has no vacancy.')],[Q('vacancy.q1','vacancy.s1','meaning','What did the hospital advertise?','An open job for a night pharmacist.','A free hotel bedroom.','A holiday closure.','A vacancy can be an unfilled job.'),Q('vacancy.q2','vacancy.s2','context','What did the receptionist check?','Whether a hotel room was available.','Whether the hospital needed a pharmacist.','Whether the driver had a job.','The hotel sense is a room free for a guest.'),Q('vacancy.q3','vacancy.s1','distinction','Which notice announces a job vacancy?','“Pharmacist position open; apply by Friday.”','“No rooms available tonight.”','“The hotel room is free.”','The first advertises an unfilled post.'),Q('vacancy.q4','vacancy.s2','word-choice','Choose the hotel meaning.','We found a vacancy at the inn after calling ahead.','The company filled its vacancy with a new engineer.','The director announced a vacant position.','Calling an inn checks whether a room is free.')]);
P('vacant','From Latin vacantem, present participle of vacare, “be empty”; it describes an unoccupied place, open job, or blank expression.',[C('vacant.s1','未占用','The flat remained vacant while its owner renovated the kitchen.','屋主翻修廚房時，公寓一直空著無人居住。','a vacant room / house / seat','Adjective: not occupied by a person, so someone else may use it.','No resident is using the flat.'),C('vacant.s2','职位空缺','The director left a vacant post after moving to another department.','主任調到另一部門後，留下了一個空缺職位。','a vacant position / post','Adjective: not filled by an employee.','No one has been appointed.'),C('vacant.s3','茫然神情','After the long exam, he stared at the clock with a vacant expression.','長時間考試後，他神情茫然地盯著時鐘。','a vacant look / expression','Adjective: showing that the mind is not thinking of anything.','His face appears blank and absent-minded.')],[M('The flat was vacant because a family had moved in and filled every room with their belongings.','The flat was occupied because a family had moved in and filled every room with their belongings.','A home in use by a family is occupied, not vacant.')],[Q('vacant.q1','vacant.s1','meaning','Why was the flat vacant?','No one lived there while it was renovated.','A family had moved into every room.','It had a new director.','Vacant means not occupied.'),Q('vacant.q2','vacant.s2','context','What happened when the director moved departments?','The post was left without an employee.','The flat was renovated.','The director stared blankly at a clock.','A vacant post is not filled by an employee.'),Q('vacant.q3','vacant.s3','distinction','What does a vacant expression suggest?','The person seems not to be thinking about anything.','The person is concentrating intensely.','The person has an available hotel room.','The mental sense describes a blank look.'),Q('vacant.q4','vacant.s1','word-choice','Which sign fits an empty rental flat?','Vacant: available for a new tenant.','Vacant: occupied by the landlord.','Vacant: post filled by an employee.','The flat is not currently occupied.')]);
P('vacate','From Latin vacare, “be empty”; the verb means leave a place or position so another can use it.',[C('vacate.s1','离开场所','Visitors must vacate the museum by closing time so staff can secure the galleries.','訪客必須在閉館時間前離開博物館，讓工作人員能鎖好展廳。','vacate a room / building / seat','Transitive verb: leave a place and make it empty for someone else.','Visitors leave the museum.'),C('vacate.s2','辞去职务','The chair agreed to vacate the post at the end of the month.','主席同意在月底離開職位。','vacate an office / post / position','Transitive verb: leave a job or position so it becomes available.','The position will be open after the chair leaves.')],[M('The visitors vacated the gallery by staying inside it after closing and refusing to leave.','The visitors occupied the gallery by staying inside it after closing and refusing to leave.','Remaining inside means occupy, not vacate, the gallery.')],[Q('vacate.q1','vacate.s1','meaning','What must museum visitors do by closing time?','Leave the building so it is empty.','Stay in the gallery all night.','Apply for the chair’s job.','Vacate means leave a place.'),Q('vacate.q2','vacate.s2','context','What did the chair agree to do?','Leave the position at month’s end.','Close the museum gallery.','Fill another person’s vacant room.','Vacate can mean leave a post so it becomes available.'),Q('vacate.q3','vacate.s1','distinction','Which action vacates a hotel room?','A guest checks out and removes their belongings.','A guest checks in and unpacks.','A clerk lists the room as occupied.','Checking out leaves the room empty for another guest.'),Q('vacate.q4','vacate.s2','word-choice','Choose the use about leaving a job.','The manager will vacate her office next month.','The family will vacate the rented house tomorrow.','The visitors vacated their seats at intermission.','The manager leaves a position or office.')]);
P('vacation','From Latin vacationem, “freedom from duty,” via Old French; it means time away, an institutional recess, or to spend a holiday.',[C('vacation.s1','休假','We took a two-week vacation after the final exams ended.','期末考結束後，我們休了兩週假。','take / go on vacation','Noun: days away from work or school, often for travel.' ,'The students are not attending classes during the break.'),C('vacation.s2','法院或大学休庭','The court will hear no new cases during its summer vacation.','法院暑假期間不會審理新案件。','court / university vacation','Noun: a period when a court or university stops its usual work.','The institution is in recess.'),C('vacation.s3','度假或腾空','They vacation on the coast each August and vacate the cottage before autumn.','他們每年八月在海岸度假，並在秋天前搬空小屋。','vacation somewhere; vacation a property','Verb: spend a holiday in a place, or leave a place empty.','The example shows holiday travel and departure from a property.')],[M('The students took a vacation during the term but attended every class as usual and had no break.','The students attended classes as usual and did not take a vacation.','A vacation is a break from work or school, not ordinary attendance.')],[Q('vacation.q1','vacation.s1','meaning','What did the students take after exams?','Two weeks away from school.','A court hearing.','A permanent job.','The first sense is time away from work or study.'),Q('vacation.q2','vacation.s2','context','What happens during the court’s summer vacation?','The court pauses its usual work and hears no new cases.','Students travel to the coast.','A family moves out of a cottage.','Institutional vacation means recess.'),Q('vacation.q3','vacation.s3','distinction','Which sentence uses vacation as a verb?','They vacation on the coast every August.','They take a vacation after exams.','The court begins its vacation in summer.','The first uses vacation to mean spend a holiday somewhere.'),Q('vacation.q4','vacation.s3','word-choice','Which sentence means “leave a place empty”?','The tenants vacationed the cottage before autumn.','The tenants vacationed on the coast.','The court vacation lasted through July.','Here the verb means leave the property vacant.')]);
P('vaccinate','From vaccine + -ate; vaccine derives from Latin vacca, “cow,” through early cowpox inoculation.',[C('vaccinate.s1','接种他人','The nurse vaccinated the children before they entered the crowded shelter.','孩子們進入擁擠的避難所前，護理師為他們接種了疫苗。','vaccinate someone against + disease','Transitive verb: inject someone with a vaccine to help protect them from disease.','The nurse gives the injection.'),C('vaccinate.s2','接受或安排接种','The clinic will vaccinate at the school gym on Saturday, and parents can book appointments there.','診所週六會在學校體育館提供接種，家長可以預約。','vaccinate at a place; get vaccinated','Verb: receive a vaccine or arrange for people to be protected by vaccination.','The second use concerns the service/arrangement.')],[M('The nurse vaccinated the children by giving them antibiotics instead of a vaccine.','The nurse treated the infection with antibiotics instead of vaccinating the children.','Vaccinate means administer a vaccine, not give antibiotics.')],[Q('vaccinate.q1','vaccinate.s1','meaning','What did the nurse do before the children entered the shelter?','Gave them vaccine injections.','Gave them antibiotics for an infection.','Tested their school uniforms.','To vaccinate someone is to inject a vaccine.'),Q('vaccinate.q2','vaccinate.s2','context','What does the clinic offer at the school gym?','A place and time where people can receive vaccines.','A court recess.','A medicine that treats every infection.','The verb can describe the vaccination service or arrangement.'),Q('vaccinate.q3','vaccinate.s1','grammar','Choose the correct pattern.','The doctor vaccinated the patient against influenza.','The doctor vaccinated against the patient influenza.','The doctor vaccination the patient for influenza.','Vaccinate takes the recipient as object, then against + disease.'),Q('vaccinate.q4','vaccinate.s2','distinction','Which sentence uses the arrangement sense?','The mobile team will vaccinate at the village hall tomorrow.','The nurse vaccinated each child yesterday.','The vaccine was stored in a cold cabinet.','The first describes a scheduled service at a place.')]);
P('vaccination','From vaccinate + -ion; historically linked to Latin vacca, “cow,” through cowpox inoculation.',[C('vaccination.s1','接种行为或处理','Vaccination at the clinic reduced the number of severe cases during the outbreak.','疫情期間，診所的疫苗接種降低了重症病例數。','vaccination against + disease; vaccination programme','Noun: the act of giving a vaccine or the treatment itself.','The preventive treatment is administered to protect people.')],[M('The vaccination exposed patients to the disease without giving any vaccine or preventive treatment.','The infection exposed patients to the disease without giving any vaccine or preventive treatment.','Vaccination is a preventive treatment with a vaccine, not exposure without it.')],[Q('vaccination.q1','vaccination.s1','meaning','What did vaccination reduce during the outbreak?','The number of severe cases.','The number of clinic rooms.','The number of trained nurses.','Vaccination is the act or treatment of giving a vaccine.'),Q('vaccination.q2','vaccination.s1','context','Which event is a vaccination?','A nurse administers a vaccine to protect a patient.','A doctor treats a broken arm with a cast.','A patient catches the illness naturally.','The treatment uses a vaccine for protection.'),Q('vaccination.q3','vaccination.s1','distinction','What does a vaccination programme organize?','Giving vaccines to people against a disease.','Repairing the clinic’s heating system.','Scheduling routine dental cleanings.','A vaccination programme arranges immunizing treatment.'),Q('vaccination.q4','vaccination.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','vaccination against measles','vaccination of a damaged bridge','vaccination to measure a temperature','Vaccination is administered to protect against disease.')]);
P('vaccine','From French vaccin, based on Latin vacca, “cow,” after early use of cowpox to prevent smallpox.',[C('vaccine.s1','制剂','The vaccine trains the immune system to recognize a protein from the virus.','疫苗使免疫系統學會辨認病毒的一種蛋白質。','a vaccine against + disease','Noun: a preparation that helps the body resist a particular disease.','The preparation trains immune defenses.'),C('vaccine.s2','接种剂量','The health programme delivered the first vaccine to remote clinics in refrigerated boxes.','衛生計畫把第一批接種用疫苗以冷藏箱送往偏遠診所。','a dose / supply of vaccine','Noun: doses of a preparation given as part of an immunization programme.','The shipment contains doses for the programme.')],[M('The vaccine weakened the immune system and trained it to attack healthy tissue instead of recognizing the virus.','The vaccine trained the immune system to recognize the virus and resist the disease.','A vaccine is intended to help the body resist a disease, not attack healthy tissue.')],[Q('vaccine.q1','vaccine.s1','meaning','What does the vaccine train the immune system to do?','Recognize a viral protein and resist disease.','Forget every infection.','Attack healthy tissue.','A vaccine prepares the body to resist a disease.'),Q('vaccine.q2','vaccine.s2','context','What was delivered to remote clinics?','Doses of vaccine in refrigerated boxes.','A supply of empty syringes only.','A package of unrelated medicines.','This use can mean vaccine doses in a programme.'),Q('vaccine.q3','vaccine.s1','distinction','Which phrase refers to the preparation itself?','a vaccine that protects against the virus','a vaccination appointment at the clinic','a clinic that stores doses','The preparation is the vaccine.'),Q('vaccine.q4','vaccine.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase about a shipment.','the first vaccine doses reached remote clinics','the vaccine trained the body to resist infection','the nurse vaccinated each child','The first describes doses delivered for a programme.')]);
P('vacillate','From Latin vacillare, “sway or waver,” often between choices or opinions.',[C('vacillate.s1','犹豫不决','The council continued to vacillate between repairing the bridge and replacing it entirely.','市議會在修橋與整座重建之間遲遲猶豫不決。','vacillate between A and B','Intransitive verb: waver between opinions or courses, unable to decide.','No option is chosen decisively.')],[M('The council vacillated between the two plans by choosing one immediately and never reconsidering it.','The council decided on one of the two plans immediately and did not vacillate.','A firm immediate choice is the opposite of wavering between options.')],[Q('vacillate.q1','vacillate.s1','meaning','What was the council doing?','Wavering between repair and replacement without deciding.','Building both plans at once.','Rejecting every bridge option immediately.','Vacillate means waver between choices.'),Q('vacillate.q2','vacillate.s1','context','Which person vacillates?','A voter changes between two candidates every time they consider them.','A voter chooses a candidate and remains certain.','A voter declines to vote without considering anyone.','The first repeatedly wavers between options.'),Q('vacillate.q3','vacillate.s1','grammar','Which construction commonly follows vacillate?','vacillate between repairing and replacing','vacillate among to repair and replace','vacillate the two choices decisively','Vacillate is intransitive and often takes between.'),Q('vacillate.q4','vacillate.s1','distinction','What is the result of vacillation?','Indecision and repeated wavering.','A final settled choice.','A guaranteed successful repair.','Vacillating keeps the decision unsettled.')]);
P('vacillation','From vacillate + -ion, “wavering”; it names repeated indecision in thought or action.',[C('vacillation.s1','反复犹豫','The manager’s vacillation delayed the launch because the team kept receiving opposite instructions.','經理反覆猶豫，讓團隊不斷收到互相矛盾的指示，發布因此延誤。','vacillation between options / in decision-making','Noun: continual wavering in opinion or action.','The manager does not settle on a direction.')],[M('Her vacillation ended the debate because she made a firm choice and never changed it.','Her decisiveness ended the debate because she made a firm choice and never changed it.','A firm unchanging choice is decisiveness, not vacillation.')],[Q('vacillation.q1','vacillation.s1','meaning','Why was the launch delayed?','The manager repeatedly changed direction and gave conflicting instructions.','The manager made one clear decision.','The team had no project to launch.','Vacillation is continual wavering in action or opinion.'),Q('vacillation.q2','vacillation.s1','context','Which behaviour shows vacillation?','A buyer alternates between two houses for weeks without choosing.','A buyer signs for one house on the first day.','A buyer decides not to purchase either house.','The repeated indecision is vacillation.'),Q('vacillation.q3','vacillation.s1','distinction','What is the opposite of vacillation in a decision?','Settled decisiveness.','Repeatedly changing one’s mind.','Asking for the same details again.','Decisiveness means choosing firmly.'),Q('vacillation.q4','vacillation.s1','word-choice','Choose the phrase using the noun naturally.','her vacillation between the two offers','her vacillatingly decision on one offer','her certain and immediate acceptance','The noun can describe wavering between choices.')]);
P('vacuole','From Latin vacuolus, “small empty space,” a diminutive of vacuus, “empty.”',[C('vacuole.s1','细胞结构','The plant cell’s vacuole stores water and dissolved substances inside a membrane.','植物細胞的液泡在膜內儲存水和溶解物質。','a vacuole in a cell; central vacuole','Noun: a small cavity inside a cell, often a large fluid-filled one in plant cells.','The structure is an enclosed storage space within the cell.')],[M('The vacuole is an organelle outside the cell membrane that pumps water into the surrounding soil.','The vacuole is a compartment inside the cell that can store water and dissolved substances.','A vacuole is inside a cell, not outside its membrane.')],[Q('vacuole.q1','vacuole.s1','meaning','Where is the plant cell’s vacuole?','Inside the cell, enclosed by a membrane.','Outside the cell membrane in the soil.','Inside the nucleus only.','A vacuole is an internal cell cavity.'),Q('vacuole.q2','vacuole.s1','context','What can the vacuole store?','Water and dissolved substances.','The whole plant cell wall.','A microscope lens.','The plant-cell vacuole stores fluid and materials.'),Q('vacuole.q3','vacuole.s1','distinction','Which structure is a vacuole?','A membrane-bound cavity within a cell.','The space between two buildings.','A tube outside a plant leaf.','The biology term names an intracellular cavity.'),Q('vacuole.q4','vacuole.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct biology sentence.','A large central vacuole helps a plant cell store water.','A vacuole is a public electricity service.','A vacuole is a person who ushers guests.','The cell organelle can serve as a water store.')]);
P('vacuous','From Latin vacuus, “empty”; figuratively it describes an empty mind or blank expression.',[C('vacuous.s1','空洞或茫然','The interviewer dismissed the vacuous slogan because it offered no explanation of the policy.','訪問者不理會那句空洞口號，因為它沒有解釋政策內容。','a vacuous statement / expression','Adjective: empty of ideas, or showing a blank expression.','The slogan contains no meaningful argument.')],[M('The vacuous slogan gave a detailed, evidence-based explanation of the policy.','The informative slogan gave a detailed, evidence-based explanation of the policy.','Detailed evidence and explanation are not vacuous or empty of ideas.')],[Q('vacuous.q1','vacuous.s1','meaning','Why was the slogan vacuous?','It contained no meaningful explanation of the policy.','It presented detailed evidence.','It gave a clear account of costs.','Vacuous means empty of ideas.'),Q('vacuous.q2','vacuous.s1','context','What does a vacuous expression show?','A blank look that seems to contain no thought.','A face showing intense concentration.','A person speaking with clear evidence.','The adjective can describe a blank expression.'),Q('vacuous.q3','vacuous.s1','distinction','Which response is vacuous?','“It is good because it is good,” with no reason.','A careful answer supported by figures.','A detailed explanation of a method.','The circular response provides no substantive ideas.'),Q('vacuous.q4','vacuous.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','a vacuous remark that said nothing meaningful','a vacuous argument supported by strong evidence','a vacuous face showing alert interest','The remark is empty of ideas.')]);
P('vacuum','From Latin vacuum, “an empty space,” from vacuus, “empty”; the word names a near-empty space, a gap, a cleaner, or cleaning by suction.',[C('vacuum.s1','物理空间','The chamber creates a vacuum so the sample is not exposed to ordinary air.','這個腔室製造真空，讓樣本不接觸一般空氣。','in a vacuum; create a vacuum','Noun: space containing no matter or almost no air.','The chamber removes most gas.'),C('vacuum.s2','缺位状态','After the principal resigned, a leadership vacuum left the school without clear direction.','校長辭職後，領導真空使學校失去明確方向。','a power / leadership vacuum','Noun: a situation where something important is missing.','No leader fills the role.'),C('vacuum.s3','吸尘器','She bought a quiet vacuum to clean the rugs without waking the baby.','她買了一台安靜的吸塵器，好清理地毯又不吵醒嬰兒。','a vacuum cleaner; turn on a vacuum','Noun: a machine that sucks up dust from floors.' ,'The machine removes dust from the rugs.'),C('vacuum.s4','用吸尘器清洁','Please vacuum the hallway before the guests arrive.','客人到達前，請用吸塵器清潔走廊。','vacuum + floor / carpet / room','Verb: clean a floor or carpet with a vacuum cleaner.','The hallway is cleaned by suction.')],[M('The cleaner vacuumed the carpet by sweeping it with a dry paintbrush and using no suction machine.','The cleaner dusted the carpet with a brush instead of vacuuming it.','Vacuum as a verb means clean with a vacuum cleaner, not with a brush.')],[Q('vacuum.q1','vacuum.s1','meaning','Why did the chamber create a vacuum?','To remove almost all air around the sample.','To add ordinary air to the sample.','To clean a rug.','A vacuum is a space with little or no matter.'),Q('vacuum.q2','vacuum.s2','context','What did the leadership vacuum leave behind?','A school without clear direction after the principal resigned.','A clean carpet.','A chamber with no air.','The figurative sense is an important role or function left empty.'),Q('vacuum.q3','vacuum.s3','distinction','Which object is a vacuum?','A machine that sucks dust from a rug.','The empty gap left by a principal.','The near-airless chamber itself.','This sense names the cleaning machine.'),Q('vacuum.q4','vacuum.s4','grammar','What does “vacuum the hallway” mean?','Clean it with a vacuum cleaner.','Create a leadership gap in it.','Remove all matter from space.','The verb means use a vacuum machine on a floor.')]);
P('vagary','From Latin vagari, “wander”; a vagary is an unpredictable turn, often of weather, mood, or fashion.',[C('vagary.s1','反复无常','The hikers packed extra layers to cope with the vagaries of mountain weather.','健行者多帶了幾層衣物，以應付山區天氣的變幻莫測。','the vagaries of + weather / fortune / mood','Noun: an unpredictable change or turn.','Mountain conditions may shift without warning.')],[M('The weather’s vagaries followed a fixed schedule and changed at exactly the same time every day.','The weather’s regular pattern followed a fixed schedule and changed at exactly the same time every day.','A predictable fixed schedule is a pattern, not a vagary.')],[Q('vagary.q1','vagary.s1','meaning','What are the vagaries of mountain weather?','Its unpredictable changes.','A fixed daily temperature schedule.','A list of hiking trails.','A vagary is an unpredictable turn.'),Q('vagary.q2','vagary.s1','context','Which is a vagary of fortune?','An unexpected reversal in someone’s circumstances.','A guaranteed salary paid on time.','A planned meeting on the calendar.','Fortune can change unpredictably.'),Q('vagary.q3','vagary.s1','distinction','Which phrase naturally uses vagary?','the vagaries of fashion','the exact timetable of a train','the fixed dimensions of a box','Fashion shifts unpredictably.'),Q('vagary.q4','vagary.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct meaning.','The gardener adapted to the vagaries of the spring weather.','The gardener relied on the vagaries of a perfectly constant climate.','The gardener measured the soil’s depth.','The weather changes in uncertain ways.')]);
P('vagrant','From Latin vagari, “wander”; the noun can mean a person without settled housing or an animal outside its usual range.',[C('vagrant.s1','漂泊者或游荡动物','A vagrant seabird appeared inland after a storm, far beyond its usual coastal range.','暴風雨後，一隻迷航海鳥出現在內陸，遠離平常的沿海活動範圍。','a vagrant bird / animal; a person without a settled home','Noun: a person who wanders without a settled home, or an animal outside its normal range.','The bird has strayed beyond its typical habitat.')],[M('The vagrant seabird was observed on its usual coastal nesting cliff within its normal range.','The resident seabird was observed on its usual coastal nesting cliff within its normal range.','A bird in its normal range is not vagrant in the animal sense.')],[Q('vagrant.q1','vagrant.s1','meaning','Why was the seabird called vagrant?','It appeared far inland, outside its usual range.','It nested on its normal coastal cliff.','It was kept in a household cage.','A vagrant animal appears outside its usual range.'),Q('vagrant.q2','vagrant.s1','context','Which animal might be described as vagrant?','A rare butterfly found far beyond its normal region.','A bird at its regular nesting site.','A fish in its ordinary pond.','The butterfly is outside its usual range.'),Q('vagrant.q3','vagrant.s1','distinction','What can vagrant mean of a person?','Someone wandering without a settled home.','Someone commuting daily from a permanent home.','A person employed as a city official.','The human sense refers to lack of settled housing.'),Q('vagrant.q4','vagrant.s1','word-choice','Choose the wildlife use.','a vagrant whale spotted in an unusual inland estuary','a resident whale in its regular migration route','a whale whose habitat has never changed','The sighting is outside the animal’s usual range.')]);
P('vague','From Latin vagus, “wandering, uncertain”; it describes unclear words or an indistinct shape or feeling.',[C('vague.s1','不明确','The contractor gave a vague estimate but did not list the materials or labour costs.','承包商只給了含糊的估價，沒有列出材料和人工費用。','a vague answer / estimate / memory','Adjective: not stated clearly or in enough detail.','The estimate lacks specific information.'),C('vague.s2','轮廓或感受微弱','A vague outline of the island appeared through the morning fog.','晨霧中隱約浮現出島嶼的輪廓。','a vague outline / feeling / resemblance','Adjective: not sharply shaped or only weakly felt.','The island’s shape is faint and indistinct.')],[M('The contractor gave a vague estimate of exactly $4,382.17 with every material and labour cost itemized.','The contractor gave a precise estimate of exactly $4,382.17 with every cost itemized.','An exact itemized figure is precise rather than vague.')],[Q('vague.q1','vague.s1','meaning','Why was the contractor’s estimate vague?','It lacked details about materials and labour.','It listed every cost to the cent.','It gave the exact start date.','Vague means not clearly or fully stated.'),Q('vague.q2','vague.s2','context','What did the island look like through fog?','Only a faint outline was visible.','Every edge was sharply visible.','The island was fully illuminated.','This sense means indistinct or weakly defined.'),Q('vague.q3','vague.s1','distinction','Which answer is vague?','“We will finish sometime soon.”','“We will finish at 3:15 on Tuesday.”','“The work needs six panels and two hours.”','The first lacks a clear time or details.'),Q('vague.q4','vague.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase about an indistinct shape.','a vague shadow behind the curtain','a vague contract that omits its price','a vague promise to call someday','The shadow has a weak, unclear outline.')]);
P('vaguely','From vague + -ly; it means not precisely or to a small degree.',[C('vaguely.s1','模糊地','I vaguely remember meeting the architect, but I cannot recall her name.','我隱約記得見過那位建築師，但想不起她的名字。','vaguely remember / resemble / understand','Adverb: not precisely, or to a small degree.','The memory is weak and incomplete.')],[M('I vaguely remember her name exactly, including every letter and the date we met.','I clearly remember her name exactly, including every letter and the date we met.','Exact recall of every detail is clear, not vague.')],[Q('vaguely.q1','vaguely.s1','meaning','How well does the speaker remember the architect?','Only indistinctly and without recalling her name.','Exactly, including every detail.','Not at all; the speaker never met her.','Vaguely means not precisely or only weakly.'),Q('vaguely.q2','vaguely.s1','context','Which person vaguely understands the rule?','Someone grasps its general idea but cannot explain the details.','Someone can state every clause exactly.','Someone has never heard of the rule.','The understanding is partial and imprecise.'),Q('vaguely.q3','vaguely.s1','grammar','What does vaguely modify in “She vaguely resembles her aunt”?','The degree of resemblance.','The aunt’s age.','The verb’s tense.','The adverb means the resemblance is slight.'),Q('vaguely.q4','vaguely.s1','distinction','Which phrase means “not in precise detail”?','vaguely describe the route','draw the route to exact scale','list each street name and turn','The first description is imprecise.')]);
P('vagueness','From vague + -ness, the quality of lacking clarity in words, shape, or thought.',[C('vagueness.s1','缺少清晰','The vagueness of the contract made it impossible to tell who was responsible for repairs.','合約含糊不清，無法判斷誰負責維修。','the vagueness of + wording / outline / thought','Noun: lack of clarity in language, shape, or thought.','The contract does not state responsibility clearly.')],[M('The vagueness of the contract removed all ambiguity by naming the repair deadline and responsible party.','The clarity of the contract removed all ambiguity by naming the repair deadline and responsible party.','Specific deadlines and responsible people remove vagueness.')],[Q('vagueness.q1','vagueness.s1','meaning','What problem did the contract’s vagueness cause?','It left repair responsibility unclear.','It clearly named the responsible person.','It guaranteed repairs by a precise date.','Vagueness is a lack of clarity.'),Q('vagueness.q2','vagueness.s1','context','Which instruction has vagueness?','“Put it somewhere safe” without saying what or where.','“Place the red folder in drawer three.”','“Turn the valve clockwise twice.”','The first lacks details.'),Q('vagueness.q3','vagueness.s1','distinction','Which is an example of vagueness in shape?','A foggy outline whose edges cannot be seen clearly.','A sharp geometric border.','A measured square with marked corners.','The outline is indistinct.'),Q('vagueness.q4','vagueness.s1','word-choice','Choose the noun for unclear wording.','vagueness in the safety rule','precision in the safety rule','the length of the safety rule','Vagueness means the wording lacks clarity.')]);
P('vaguest','Superlative of vague, formed with -est, meaning more unclear than any other item in a comparison.',[C('vaguest.s1','最高级比较','Of the three witness accounts, Lee’s was the vaguest because it gave no time, place, or description.','三份證詞中，李的那份最含糊，沒有提供時間、地點或描述。','the vaguest + noun; the vaguest of + group','Superlative adjective: the least clear or detailed in a comparison.','Lee’s account has less detail than the other two.')],[M('Lee’s was the vaguest account because it gave the exact time, address, and a detailed description.','Lee’s was the clearest account because it gave the exact time, address, and a detailed description.','Exact time, address, and detail make an account clear, not the vaguest.')],[Q('vaguest.q1','vaguest.s1','meaning','Why was Lee’s account the vaguest?','It omitted the time, place, and description.','It gave exact time, address, and details.','It was the longest account.','Vaguest is the superlative for least clear.'),Q('vaguest.q2','vaguest.s1','context','Which instruction is the vaguest of three?','“Do the task sometime” with no task details.','“Submit the signed form by noon Friday.”','“Move the table two metres left.”','The first gives the least specific direction.'),Q('vaguest.q3','vaguest.s1','grammar','How is vaguest formed?','Vague + -est for the highest degree in a comparison.','Vague + -ly to form an adverb.','Vague + -ness to form a noun.','The suffix -est marks the superlative.'),Q('vaguest.q4','vaguest.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses vaguest correctly?','Of the four proposals, the last gives the vaguest budget.','The last proposal is vague than the first.','The last proposal is the vaguely budget.','The superlative compares the last proposal with the full group.')]);
P('vain','From Old French vain, from Latin vanus, “empty”; it means futile or excessively proud.',[C('vain.s1','徒劳','They searched in vain for the missing key until the caretaker returned with a spare.','他們徒勞地尋找失蹤的鑰匙，直到管理員帶著備用鑰匙回來。','in vain; a vain attempt','Adjective: not producing the result wanted.','The search does not find the key.'),C('vain.s2','自负','The vain actor checked his reflection before every interview.','那位自負的演員每次訪問前都要照鏡子。','vain about + appearance / success','Adjective: too proud of one’s appearance or achievements.','He gives excessive attention to his own image.')],[M('They searched in vain and found the missing key on their first careful look.','They searched successfully and found the missing key on their first careful look.','A search that finds the key is not in vain.')],[Q('vain.q1','vain.s1','meaning','Why was the search in vain?','It did not find the missing key.','It found the key immediately.','The caretaker had the key all along.','In vain describes an effort that fails.'),Q('vain.q2','vain.s2','context','Why was the actor described as vain?','He was excessively concerned with his appearance.','He avoided looking at himself.','He searched unsuccessfully for a key.','The second sense means too proud of appearance or achievement.'),Q('vain.q3','vain.s1','distinction','Which phrase means an effort was futile?','a vain attempt to restart the dead engine','a vain actor admiring his portrait','a successful attempt that fixed the engine','The first attempt produces no desired result.'),Q('vain.q4','vain.s2','word-choice','Choose the use about excessive pride.','She was vain about her awards and demanded constant praise.','They tried in vain to reach the island.','His efforts were vain because the file was gone.','Her pride in her achievements is excessive.')]);
P('valiant','From Old French vaillant, based on valoir, “be worth”; it describes courage or a praiseworthy effort.',[C('valiant.s1','英勇','The valiant medic crossed the exposed road to reach the injured soldiers.','勇敢的軍醫穿越暴露的道路，去救助受傷士兵。','a valiant soldier / defence / act','Adjective: showing great courage, especially in battle.','The medic faces danger to help others.'),C('valiant.s2','努力可嘉','The team made a valiant attempt to finish the repairs before the storm arrived.','團隊努力在暴風雨到來前完成修繕，雖未必成功但值得稱許。','a valiant effort / attempt','Adjective: deserving praise for trying hard against difficulties.','The effort is courageous despite obstacles.')],[M('The valiant medic hid safely indoors and refused to help anyone in danger.','The cautious medic stayed safely indoors and did not attempt the rescue.','Refusing to face danger does not show the courage meant by valiant.')],[Q('valiant.q1','valiant.s1','meaning','Why was the medic valiant?','The medic faced danger to reach the injured soldiers.','The medic refused to leave a safe room.','The medic caused the storm.','Valiant describes great courage in danger.'),Q('valiant.q2','valiant.s2','context','Why was the repair attempt valiant?','The team tried hard despite difficult odds.','The team never began the work.','The storm arrived after every repair was finished early.','A valiant effort deserves praise even if success is uncertain.'),Q('valiant.q3','valiant.s1','distinction','Which act is valiant?','A rescuer enters a dangerous area to help trapped people.','A bystander avoids a safe conversation.','A worker completes an ordinary task at a desk.','The rescue requires courage in danger.'),Q('valiant.q4','valiant.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase about a praiseworthy effort.','a valiant attempt to save the failing project','a completed task requiring no difficulty','a careless decision made without trying','The attempt is commendable despite difficulty.')]);
P('valid','From Latin validus, “strong, effective”; it describes something officially acceptable or logically sound.',[C('valid.s1','法律或官方有效','The permit remains valid until the end of June, so the crew may continue working.','許可證到六月底仍有效，因此施工隊可以繼續工作。','a valid permit / passport / agreement','Adjective: officially acceptable and still in force.','The permit has not expired.'),C('valid.s2','论据成立','Her objection was valid because the figures in the report used the wrong exchange rate.','她的反對理由成立，因為報告中的數字用了錯誤匯率。','a valid reason / argument / point','Adjective: based on truth or good reasoning.','The objection follows from a factual error.')],[M('The permit was valid after its expiry date had passed and the issuing office had cancelled it.','The permit was invalid after its expiry date had passed and the issuing office had cancelled it.','An expired and cancelled permit is no longer officially in force.')],[Q('valid.q1','valid.s1','meaning','Why may the crew keep working?','The permit is still in force and has not expired.','The permit was cancelled last year.','The crew has no permit.','Valid means officially acceptable and current.'),Q('valid.q2','valid.s2','context','Why was her objection valid?','The report used an incorrect exchange rate.','The figures were accurate and the rate was current.','She objected without giving a reason.','A valid argument is supported by sound evidence.'),Q('valid.q3','valid.s1','distinction','Which document is valid?','A passport that has not expired or been cancelled.','An expired permit.','A cancelled agreement.','The document remains officially acceptable.'),Q('valid.q4','valid.s2','word-choice','Choose the use about good reasoning.','That is a valid reason to delay the vote.','The permit is valid through June.','The passport remains valid abroad.','The reason is supported by facts.')]);
P('validate','From Latin validus, “strong”; the verb means prove a claim true or make a document legally acceptable.',[C('validate.s1','证实理论','The new measurements validate the theory that the bridge flexes more in cold weather.','新的測量結果證實了橋梁在寒冷天氣下彎曲較多的理論。','validate a finding / theory / result','Transitive verb: provide evidence that a belief or theory is true.','The measurements support the theory.'),C('validate.s2','使文件生效','Both parties must sign the form to validate the agreement.','雙方都必須在表格上簽名，協議才具法律效力。','validate a ticket / document / agreement','Transitive verb: make a document or agreement legally accepted.','The signatures give the agreement legal force.')],[M('The measurements validated the theory even though every result contradicted its prediction.','The measurements contradicted the theory because every result opposed its prediction.','Evidence that contradicts a theory does not validate it.')],[Q('validate.q1','validate.s1','meaning','What did the new measurements do?','Provided evidence supporting the bridge theory.','Cancelled the bridge permit.','Made a form legally binding.','Validate can mean prove a belief or theory true.'),Q('validate.q2','validate.s2','context','Why must both parties sign the form?','Their signatures make the agreement legally accepted.','The signatures measure bridge movement.','The form becomes a scientific theory.','This sense means give legal validity to a document.'),Q('validate.q3','validate.s1','distinction','Which result validates a hypothesis?','Repeated tests produce the outcome it predicted.','Every test gives the opposite outcome.','No test is performed.','Supporting evidence validates the claim.'),Q('validate.q4','validate.s2','word-choice','Choose the legal-document use.','The clerk validated the parking ticket at the desk.','The experiment validated the scientist’s prediction.','The data validated the theory.','The clerk makes the ticket officially accepted.')]);
P('validity','From valid + -ity, the state of being officially accepted or logically well-founded.',[C('validity.s1','法律效力','The lawyer questioned the validity of the contract because one required signature was missing.','因缺少一個必要簽名，律師質疑合約的法律效力。','the validity of a permit / contract','Noun: the state of being legally or officially accepted.','The missing signature may prevent legal acceptance.'),C('validity.s2','论证可靠性','Researchers tested the validity of the survey by comparing its results with independent interviews.','研究人員將問卷結果與獨立訪談比較，以檢驗其可靠性。','the validity of a claim / argument / test','Noun: the quality of being based on truth and good reasons.','Independent evidence checks whether the conclusions are justified.')],[M('The survey’s validity was confirmed because its results contradicted every independent interview.','The survey’s validity was questioned because its results contradicted every independent interview.','Contradictory evidence gives reason to question validity, not confirm it.')],[Q('validity.q1','validity.s1','meaning','Why did the lawyer question the contract’s validity?','A required signature was missing.','Every signature was present and accepted.','The contract was a survey.','This sense concerns legal or official acceptance.'),Q('validity.q2','validity.s2','context','How did researchers test the survey’s validity?','They compared it with independent interviews.','They checked whether its cover was colourful.','They cancelled the interview programme.','This sense asks whether results are well-founded.'),Q('validity.q3','validity.s1','distinction','Which question concerns legal validity?','Was the permit properly signed and still in force?','Did the survey sample represent the population?','Did the argument use accurate evidence?','The permit question concerns official standing.'),Q('validity.q4','validity.s2','word-choice','Choose the use about the soundness of evidence.','The study examined the validity of its conclusions.','The court ruled on the validity of the contract.','The clerk checked the permit’s validity date.','The study tests whether conclusions follow from good evidence.')]);
P('valley','From Old French valée, “valley,” based on Latin vallis; it can mean low land or the region drained by a river.',[C('valley.s1','地形','A narrow valley lay between the two ridges, with a stream running along its floor.','兩道山脊之間有一條狹窄山谷，溪流沿谷底而行。','a valley between / below hills','Noun: low land lying between hills or mountains.','The stream occupies the low ground.'),C('valley.s2','流域','The entire valley drains into the same river, including farms beyond the visible hills.','包括可見山丘外的農田在內，整個流域的水都流入同一條河。','the valley of + river','Noun: the whole region drained by one river system.','The region is defined by where its water flows.')],[M('The valley lay on the mountain summit, higher than both ridges surrounding it.','The valley lay between the two ridges, lower than the surrounding hills.','A valley is low land between higher ground.')],[Q('valley.q1','valley.s1','meaning','Where was the narrow valley?','Between two ridges, with a stream on its floor.','On top of the tallest ridge.','Far above the surrounding hills.','The landform is low ground between hills.'),Q('valley.q2','valley.s2','context','What defines the whole river valley in the second sense?','The region whose water drains into that river system.','Only the visible stream bank.','The mountain summit where rain first falls.','A drainage basin includes all land feeding the river.'),Q('valley.q3','valley.s1','distinction','Which place is a valley?','Low ground running between two mountain slopes.','A peak above all nearby land.','A flat roof on a city building.','A valley sits below surrounding hills.'),Q('valley.q4','valley.s2','word-choice','Choose the phrase about a drainage region.','the valley drained by the upper river','a valley floor between two slopes','a narrow hollow below the ridge','The first refers to the full river-drained region.')]);
P('valor','From Latin valor, “worth or bravery,” through Old French; in modern use it chiefly means courage in danger.',[C('valor.s1','英勇','The memorial honours the valor of medics who treated wounded people under fire.','紀念碑表彰了在砲火下救治傷者的醫護人員的英勇。','show / display / honour valor','Noun: bravery in the face of danger, especially in war.','The medics act courageously under fire.')],[M('The citation praised his valor because he avoided danger and left the wounded without help.','The citation praised his caution because he avoided danger and left the wounded without help.','Avoiding danger while abandoning the injured is not the courage meant by valor.')],[Q('valor.q1','valor.s1','meaning','Why did the memorial honour the medics’ valor?','They treated wounded people under fire.','They avoided danger and left the injured.','They organized a festival after the war.','Valor means bravery while facing danger.'),Q('valor.q2','valor.s1','context','Which act shows valor?','A firefighter enters a dangerous building to rescue someone.','A spectator watches safely from a distance.','A clerk files routine paperwork.','The rescue requires courage in danger.'),Q('valor.q3','valor.s1','distinction','In what setting is valor especially associated?','Courageous action in war or battle.','A quiet household chore.','A price estimate for a painting.','Valor traditionally refers to bravery, particularly in war.'),Q('valor.q4','valor.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','a medal awarded for valor under fire','valor measured as the cost of a bridge','a valor of water used each month','Valor names bravery, not a quantity or price.')]);
P('valorous','From valor + -ous, a formal or literary adjective meaning full of courage.',[C('valorous.s1','勇敢','The chronicle tells of a valorous defence of the mountain pass against a much larger force.','編年史記載了面對大得多的敵軍時，守軍英勇防守山口的事蹟。','a valorous defence / deed / soldier','Adjective: brave, in a formal or literary style.','The defenders show courage despite being outnumbered.')],[M('The chronicle called the defenders valorous because they fled at the first sign of danger and left the pass unguarded.','The chronicle called the defenders fearful because they fled at the first sign of danger and left the pass unguarded.','Fleeing at the first sign of danger does not show the courage valorous describes.')],[Q('valorous.q1','valorous.s1','meaning','Why was the defence called valorous?','The defenders courageously held the pass against a larger force.','They abandoned the pass at the first danger.','They repaired the valley road.','Valorous means brave, especially in a formal account.'),Q('valorous.q2','valorous.s1','context','Which deed is valorous?','A medic crosses an exposed field to help the injured.','A soldier refuses to assist anyone.','A clerk checks a routine form.','The medic acts bravely despite danger.'),Q('valorous.q3','valorous.s1','distinction','What style does valorous often have?','Formal or literary.','Technical computing only.','Casual slang only.','The adjective is a formal alternative for brave.'),Q('valorous.q4','valorous.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','a valorous rescue under fire','a valorous retreat from every safe task','a valorous price estimate','The rescue shows courage in danger.')]);
P('valour','British spelling of valor, from Latin valor through Old French; it means bravery, especially in battle.',[C('valour.s1','英勇','The official citation recognized the pilot’s valour during the dangerous evacuation.','官方嘉獎令肯定了飛行員在危險撤離行動中的英勇。','show / award / recognize valour','Noun: bravery, especially in battle; the British spelling is valour.','The pilot acted courageously in danger.')],[M('The citation praised her valour because she abandoned the passengers at the first sign of danger.','The citation criticized her cowardice because she abandoned the passengers at the first sign of danger.','Abandoning people to avoid danger is not valour.')],[Q('valour.q1','valour.s1','meaning','What did the citation recognize?','The pilot’s bravery during a dangerous evacuation.','The pilot’s ability to estimate a price.','A public electricity service.','Valour means courage, especially in battle.'),Q('valour.q2','valour.s1','spelling','Which spelling is British English?','valour','valor only','valoure','Valour is the British spelling; valor is American.'),Q('valour.q3','valour.s1','context','Which act could be praised as valour?','A rescue pilot flies into danger to evacuate people.','A pilot refuses to fly and leaves passengers behind.','A clerk signs a routine form.','The rescue requires bravery.'),Q('valour.q4','valour.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses valour correctly?','a story of valour in battle','a bill for household valour','a valour of water in the reservoir','Valour is bravery, not a service or measurement.')]);
P('valse','Borrowed from French valse, “waltz”; as a verb it means to move in the turning step of a waltz.',[C('valse.s1','舞蹈','The dancers valse slowly around the room while the orchestra plays a waltz.','樂團演奏圓舞曲時，舞者在房間裡緩緩跳起華爾滋。','valse to / around + music or floor','Verb: dance or move with the turning step of a waltz.','The dancers turn in the characteristic waltz step.')],[M('The couple valse across the floor by standing still and never taking a turning step.','The couple waltz across the floor by moving in turning steps.','Valse means dance a turning waltz step, not remain still.')],[Q('valse.q1','valse.s1','meaning','How did the dancers move?','They turned slowly in waltz steps.','They stood still throughout the music.','They ran in a straight line.','Valse means to waltz or move in its turning step.'),Q('valse.q2','valse.s1','context','What music accompanies the dancers?','A waltz played by the orchestra.','A speech with no music.','A marching song with no turns.','The verb describes dancing to waltz music.'),Q('valse.q3','valse.s1','distinction','Which action is to valse?','Turning across the floor in three-beat dance steps.','Sitting motionless through the song.','Jumping straight up without moving.','The turning step is characteristic of a waltz.'),Q('valse.q4','valse.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural sentence.','The pair began to valse when the orchestra started the waltz.','The pair valse by sitting down and stopping the music.','The pair valse a kitchen utensil.','The verb refers to waltz dancing.')]);
P('valuable','From value + -able; it means high in monetary worth or useful and important.',[C('valuable.s1','昂贵或值钱','The museum moved the valuable necklace into a locked display case.','博物館把這條貴重項鍊移進上鎖的展示櫃。','a valuable object / collection','Adjective: worth a lot of money.','The necklace has a high monetary price.'),C('valuable.s2','有帮助或重要','The engineer’s field notes were valuable to the rescue team because they mapped the hidden access road.','工程師的實地筆記為救援隊提供重要幫助，標出了隱蔽道路。','valuable to + person / project','Adjective: very useful, helpful, or important.','The notes provide information useful to the rescue.')],[M('The valuable necklace was worthless and had no monetary or practical worth at all.','The worthless necklace had no monetary or practical worth at all.','Something with no worth is worthless rather than valuable.')],[Q('valuable.q1','valuable.s1','meaning','Why was the necklace placed in a locked case?','It was worth a lot of money.','It had no value or use.','It was a map of an access road.','Valuable can mean high in monetary worth.'),Q('valuable.q2','valuable.s2','context','Why were the field notes valuable to rescuers?','They showed a hidden access road.','They were made of expensive gold.','They described a necklace’s price.','The notes were useful to the rescue operation.'),Q('valuable.q3','valuable.s1','distinction','Which item is valuable in price?','A rare painting sold for a large sum.','A free map that saves hikers time.','A low-cost pen with no special worth.','The painting has a high monetary price.'),Q('valuable.q4','valuable.s2','word-choice','Choose the use meaning “important and helpful.”','Her advice was valuable to the new team.','The valuable ring cost thousands of dollars.','The necklace was stored in a vault.','The advice provides helpful guidance.')]);
P('valuation','From value + -ation, the process or result of estimating monetary or other worth.',[C('valuation.s1','估值','The insurer requested a new valuation of the damaged warehouse before approving the claim.','保險公司要求先重新估算受損倉庫的價值，再核准理賠。','a valuation of + property / asset','Noun: an estimate of worth or the process of making that estimate.','The insurer needs a current estimate of monetary worth.')],[M('The valuation estimated the warehouse’s worth, but it gave no estimate and did not assess any value.','The inspection described the warehouse’s condition but did not provide a valuation.','A valuation must estimate worth; a condition report alone is not one.')],[Q('valuation.q1','valuation.s1','meaning','Why did the insurer request a valuation?','To estimate the damaged warehouse’s worth.','To schedule a holiday.','To measure the building’s colour.','A valuation estimates monetary or other value.'),Q('valuation.q2','valuation.s1','context','Which report contains a valuation?','An appraiser estimates a house at $420,000.','An inspector lists cracks but gives no estimate.','A tenant describes the rooms.','The appraiser provides an estimate of worth.'),Q('valuation.q3','valuation.s1','distinction','What does a valuation focus on?','How much an asset is worth.','How many people use a service.','How a word is normally used.','Valuation is an estimate or process of assessing worth.'),Q('valuation.q4','valuation.s1','word-choice','Choose the phrase using valuation correctly.','the valuation of the damaged machinery','the vaccination of the damaged machinery','the vacation of the machinery’s owner','The appraiser assesses the machinery’s worth.')]);
P('value','From Old French value, from valoir, “be worth”; as noun and verb it concerns worth, principles, esteem, or appraisal.',[C('value.s1','价值','The old map has little market value but great value to historians studying the lost road.','這張舊地圖市場價格不高，卻對研究失落道路的歷史學家很有價值。','the value of + object / amount','Noun: how much something is worth in money or usefulness.','The map’s usefulness to historians is high despite low price.'),C('value.s2','价值观','Honesty is a value that the family teaches through everyday decisions.','誠實是這個家庭透過日常決定教給孩子的一項價值觀。','a personal / social value','Noun: a belief about what is right and important in life.','Honesty guides the family’s choices.'),C('value.s3','重视','The editor values clear evidence more than a dramatic headline.','編輯重視清楚的證據勝過聳動標題。','value + person / quality / contribution','Verb: think someone or something is important.','The editor gives evidence high importance.'),C('value.s4','估价','The appraiser valued the vase at $800 after examining its maker’s mark.','估價師檢查製作者標記後，將花瓶估值為八百美元。','value + object at + amount','Verb: decide how much money something is worth.','The appraiser assigns a monetary estimate.')],[M('The appraiser valued the vase at $800 without estimating or stating any amount for it.','The appraiser described the vase but did not value it.','To value an object in this sense is to estimate its monetary worth.')],[Q('value.q1','value.s1','meaning','Why was the old map valuable to historians?','It was useful for studying the lost road.','It had the highest market price in the museum.','It taught the family honesty.','Value can mean usefulness as well as money worth.'),Q('value.q2','value.s2','context','What does honesty mean as a family value?','A belief about what is right and important.','A price assigned to a vase.','A dramatic newspaper headline.','Values are beliefs that guide decisions.'),Q('value.q3','value.s3','distinction','What does the editor value?','Clear evidence, which the editor considers important.','A vase priced at eight hundred dollars.','A map’s market price only.','The verb value means think something is important.'),Q('value.q4','value.s4','word-choice','What did the appraiser do?','Estimated the vase’s worth at $800.','Respected the editor’s evidence.','Taught a family belief.','Value as a verb can mean assess monetary worth.')]);
P('valued','From value + -ed; it describes someone highly regarded or an object assigned a price.',[C('valued.s1','受重视或估价','A valued colleague helped the new staff settle in during their first week.','一位受重視的同事在新員工第一週協助他們適應。','a valued colleague / member; be valued at + price','Adjective: highly regarded, or assigned a particular worth.','The colleague is appreciated by the team.')],[M('The valued colleague was ignored by everyone and no one considered the colleague important.','The disregarded colleague was ignored by everyone and no one considered the colleague important.','Someone ignored and not considered important is not valued by the group.')],[Q('valued.q1','valued.s1','meaning','Why was the colleague valued?','The team appreciated the help given to new staff.','The colleague was ignored by everyone.','The colleague was assigned a legal permit.','Valued means highly regarded.'),Q('valued.q2','valued.s1','context','What does “the painting was valued at $2,000” mean?','Someone estimated its worth at that amount.','The painting was praised as a colleague.','The painting sold for no price.','Valued at gives an estimated monetary worth.'),Q('valued.q3','valued.s1','distinction','Which person is valued?','A mentor whose advice is appreciated by the team.','A stranger whose contribution is unknown.','A discarded tool no one uses.','The mentor is regarded as important.'),Q('valued.q4','valued.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','a valued member of the rescue team','a valued member ignored by every teammate','a valued price with no estimate','The first describes someone highly regarded.')]);
P('valued at','Past-participle phrase from value + at, used to state an estimated worth.',[C('valued at.s1','估计价格','The restored theatre is valued at six million dollars by the city’s property office.','市政府房產部門估計修復後的劇院價值六百萬美元。','be valued at + amount','Passive verb phrase: be estimated or judged to be worth a particular amount.','The amount is the official estimate, not necessarily a sale price.')],[M('The theatre is valued at six million dollars, which means the property office assigned no estimate at all.','The theatre has no valuation because the property office assigned no estimate at all.','A stated figure after valued at is an estimate of worth.')],[Q('valued at.q1','valued at.s1','meaning','What does “valued at six million dollars” state?','An estimated worth of six million dollars.','A confirmed sale for one dollar.','The building’s yearly attendance.','Valued at introduces an estimated amount.'),Q('valued at.q2','valued at.s1','context','How much is the restored theatre estimated to be worth?','Six million dollars.','Six thousand visitors.','No amount was estimated.','The phrase states the estimate.'),Q('valued at.q3','valued at.s1','grammar','Choose the correct construction.','The sculpture is valued at $4,000.','The sculpture is valued for $4,000 at.','The sculpture valued $4,000 at is.','The standard phrase is be valued at + amount.'),Q('valued at.q4','valued at.s1','distinction','Does “valued at $4,000” necessarily mean it sold for that amount?','No; it states an estimated worth.','Yes; it always records a completed sale.','No; it means no one estimated the worth.','Valued at reports an estimate, not necessarily a sale.')]);
P('valve','From Latin valva, “leaf of a folding door”; it names a flow-control device, a body flap, or an old radio tube.',[C('valve.s1','流体控制','Turn the valve slowly to stop water from entering the damaged pipe.','慢慢轉動閥門，阻止水流進受損管道。','open / close / turn a valve','Noun: a device that lets liquid or gas flow one way or stops it.','The valve controls water flow.'),C('valve.s2','心脏结构','A heart valve keeps blood moving in the correct direction between chambers.','心臟瓣膜使血液在心腔之間朝正確方向流動。','a heart / vein valve','Noun: a flap in the heart or a vein that keeps blood flowing one way.','The flap prevents backward flow.'),C('valve.s3','旧式电子管','The repairer replaced a glass valve in the vintage radio before testing its sound.','維修員更換古董收音機中的玻璃電子管後，才測試音效。','a radio valve (British; US tube)','Noun: a glass tube in an old radio that controls electric current.','The component regulates current in the radio.')],[M('The plumber opened the valve to stop water flow, then claimed that valves make water flow in both directions without control.','The plumber closed the valve to stop water flow.','A valve regulates or stops flow; it does not mean uncontrolled two-way flow.')],[Q('valve.q1','valve.s1','meaning','What did the plumber turn to stop water entering the pipe?','A flow-control valve.','A heart chamber.','A radio speaker.','This sense controls liquid or gas flow.'),Q('valve.q2','valve.s2','context','What does a heart valve do?','Keeps blood moving in one direction.','Stores water in a pipe.','Amplifies sound in a radio.','The body flap prevents backward blood flow.'),Q('valve.q3','valve.s3','distinction','Which component might be found in a vintage radio?','A glass valve that controls electric current.','A vein flap that directs blood.','A water pipe shutoff only.','The old radio sense is a glass electronic tube.'),Q('valve.q4','valve.s1','word-choice','Choose the plumbing use.','Close the valve before repairing the pipe.','Replace the radio valve to restore the old set.','An injured valve altered blood flow.','The plumbing valve stops water flow.')]);
P('van','Shortened from caravan for a box-shaped vehicle; van can also mean the leading position of a movement.',[C('van.s1','车辆','The museum van carried a crate of paintings to the conservation centre.','博物館的廂型車把一箱畫作運到保存中心。','a delivery / passenger van','Noun: a box-shaped vehicle for goods or a small group of people.','The vehicle transports the paintings.'),C('van.s2','运动先锋','The poet stood in the van of a movement that challenged conventional verse.','這位詩人站在挑戰傳統詩體的運動前列。','in the van of + movement / change','Noun: the leading position in a new movement or development.','The poet is at the forefront.')],[M('The museum van carried the paintings in a small animal that fit in a pocket.','The museum van carried the paintings in a box-shaped vehicle.','A van is a motor vehicle, not a tiny animal.')],[Q('van.q1','van.s1','meaning','What carried the paintings to the conservation centre?','A box-shaped vehicle.','A leading group of poets.','A heart valve.','The vehicle sense is a van used for goods or passengers.'),Q('van.q2','van.s2','context','What did the poet’s position in the van mean?','The poet was at the forefront of a new movement.','The poet drove the museum’s delivery vehicle.','The poet was behind every other writer.','The figurative sense is the leading position.'),Q('van.q3','van.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses van for a vehicle?','A van delivered the paintings to the museum.','The poet was in the van of the new school.','The movement placed its leaders in the van.','The first names the transport vehicle.'),Q('van.q4','van.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','She worked in the van of the campaign for clean water.','She drove a van to deliver supplies.','The van carried boxes to the camp.','The phrase means at the front of a movement.')]);
P('vancouver','Named for British naval officer George Vancouver, whose 1790s expeditions charted parts of the Pacific coast.',[C('vancouver.s1','地名','Vancouver lies on the Pacific coast of British Columbia and is the province’s largest city.','溫哥華位於卑詩省太平洋沿岸，是該省最大的城市。','Vancouver, British Columbia','Proper noun: the largest city in British Columbia, on Canada’s Pacific coast.','The place is identified by province and coast.')],[M('Vancouver is the largest city in Alberta, far from British Columbia and Canada’s Pacific coast.','Vancouver is the largest city in British Columbia, on Canada’s Pacific coast.','The source locates Vancouver in British Columbia on the Pacific coast.')],[Q('vancouver.q1','vancouver.s1','meaning','Where is Vancouver?','On the Pacific coast of British Columbia.','In Alberta’s mountain interior.','On the Atlantic coast of the United States.','Vancouver is a city in British Columbia, Canada.'),Q('vancouver.q2','vancouver.s1','context','Which province is home to Vancouver?','British Columbia.','Alberta.','Quebec.','The city is the largest in British Columbia.'),Q('vancouver.q3','vancouver.s1','distinction','Which description identifies Vancouver in this entry?','A Pacific-coast city in British Columbia.','A Great Basin Indigenous nation.','A small town in the Atlantic provinces.','Its defining location is British Columbia’s Pacific coast.'),Q('vancouver.q4','vancouver.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate sentence.','Vancouver is a major city on Canada’s Pacific coast.','Vancouver is the largest city in Alberta.','Vancouver is a British city on the North Sea.','The city lies in British Columbia on the Pacific.')]);
P('vandal','From Latin Vandalus, the name of an ancient Germanic people, later applied to someone who deliberately damages property.',[C('vandal.s1','故意破坏者','A vandal scratched the station’s new windows overnight, and police asked nearby shops for camera footage.','破壞者夜裡刮傷了車站的新窗戶，警方請附近商店提供監視畫面。','a vandal damages / defaces property','Noun: someone who intentionally ruins or defaces property.','The scratching is deliberate damage.')],[M('The museum called the careful conservator a vandal because she restored the damaged painting without harming it.','The museum called the person who deliberately scratched the painting a vandal.','A conservator restoring an object does not intentionally deface or ruin it.')],[Q('vandal.q1','vandal.s1','meaning','What did the vandal do at the station?','Deliberately scratched the new windows.','Restored the windows carefully.','Installed a camera for the police.','A vandal intentionally damages property.'),Q('vandal.q2','vandal.s1','context','Who would be called a vandal?','Someone who deliberately sprays paint over a public sign.','A worker who repairs the sign.','A visitor who reads the sign.','The first intentionally defaces property.'),Q('vandal.q3','vandal.s1','distinction','Which action is vandalism by a vandal?','Breaking a bus shelter window on purpose.','Replacing a broken shelter window.','Reporting damage to the shelter.','Intentional destruction is vandalism.'),Q('vandal.q4','vandal.s1','word-choice','Choose the sentence using vandal correctly.','A vandal damaged the school gate overnight.','The vandal repaired the gate and paid for the parts.','The vandal measured the gate for a renovation.','The first describes intentional property damage.')]);
P('vandalism','From vandal + -ism; it names deliberate damage to public or private property.',[C('vandalism.s1','财物破坏','The council installed brighter lights to discourage vandalism in the underground car park.','市議會加裝更亮的燈，以遏止地下停車場的蓄意破壞行為。','acts of / prevent / report vandalism','Noun: deliberate damage to public or private property.','The lights aim to deter intentional damage.')],[M('The report classified the careful restoration of the mural as vandalism, although no paint or surface was damaged.','The report classified the deliberate destruction of the mural as vandalism.','Vandalism requires intentional damage, not careful restoration.')],[Q('vandalism.q1','vandalism.s1','meaning','Why did the council install brighter lights?','To discourage deliberate damage to the car park.','To celebrate a mural restoration.','To increase the number of parking spaces.','Vandalism is intentional damage to property.'),Q('vandalism.q2','vandalism.s1','context','Which incident is vandalism?','Someone deliberately smashes a bus stop panel.','A storm accidentally breaks a panel.','A technician replaces a cracked panel.','Vandalism is deliberate, not accidental, damage.'),Q('vandalism.q3','vandalism.s1','distinction','What property can vandalism affect?','Public or privately owned property.','Only ancient monuments.','Only a person’s feelings.','The definition includes both public and private property.'),Q('vandalism.q4','vandalism.s1','word-choice','Choose the phrase about preventing property damage.','a camera installed to deter vandalism','a camera that vandalism operated','a repair that deliberately destroys the sign','A camera may discourage acts of vandalism.')]);
P('vanguard','From Old French avant-garde, literally “front guard,” later shortened in English; it can mean leaders or an advance military group.',[C('vanguard.s1','发展前沿','The laboratory’s team was in the vanguard of research on low-cost water filters.','這個實驗室團隊處於低成本濾水器研究的前沿。','in the vanguard of + movement / research','Noun: people or ideas leading a development or movement.','The team is among the leaders in the field.'),C('vanguard.s2','先遣部队','The vanguard crossed the ridge before the main force began its march.','主力部隊出發前，先遣部隊已越過山脊。','the vanguard of an army / group','Noun: the part of an army or group that goes first.','This group advances ahead of the main body.')],[M('The vanguard crossed the ridge last, long after the main force had passed.','The rearguard crossed the ridge last, long after the main force had passed.','A group that goes first is the vanguard; one that follows last is the rearguard.')],[Q('vanguard.q1','vanguard.s1','meaning','Why was the laboratory in the vanguard?','Its team led research on low-cost water filters.','It followed every development years later.','It crossed a ridge before an army.','The figurative vanguard leads a field or movement.'),Q('vanguard.q2','vanguard.s2','context','What did the vanguard do in the march?','Crossed the ridge ahead of the main force.','Followed the main force from behind.','Stayed in the laboratory.','The military vanguard goes first.'),Q('vanguard.q3','vanguard.s1','distinction','Which group is in the vanguard of a new movement?','Artists who pioneer its methods and ideas.','People who adopt the movement only after it ends.','A group guarding the rear of a convoy.','The leaders are at the forefront.'),Q('vanguard.q4','vanguard.s2','word-choice','Choose the military use.','The vanguard advanced ahead of the main army.','The vanguard pioneered a new style of poetry.','The research team led a new movement.','The first describes the leading part of a force.')]);
P('vanish','From Old French esvanir, from Latin evanescere, “fade away”; it means become unseen or cease to exist.',[C('vanish.s1','消失不见','The fox vanished into the tall grass before the photographer could focus the lens.','攝影師還來不及對焦，狐狸就消失在高草叢中。','vanish from sight / into + place','Intransitive verb: go away so people can no longer see you.','The fox is hidden from view.'),C('vanish.s2','不复存在','Several local dialects may vanish if children stop learning them at home.','如果孩子不再在家中學習，幾種地方方言可能會消失。','vanish from existence / records','Intransitive verb: stop existing.','The dialects would no longer be spoken.')],[M('The fox vanished into the grass but remained fully visible in the photographer’s clear view.','The fox stayed visible in the grass and did not vanish from sight.','Something still fully visible has not vanished from view.')],[Q('vanish.q1','vanish.s1','meaning','What happened to the fox?','It went out of sight in the tall grass.','It became a local dialect.','It stayed clearly visible in the lens.','This sense means become impossible to see.'),Q('vanish.q2','vanish.s2','context','What may happen to the local dialects?','They may cease to exist if children stop learning them.','They may become more visible in the grass.','They may turn into written records.','The second sense is stop existing.'),Q('vanish.q3','vanish.s1','distinction','Which object vanished from sight?','A boat disappeared behind the fog.','A custom stopped being practiced over centuries.','A language ceased to exist.','The boat can no longer be seen.'),Q('vanish.q4','vanish.s2','word-choice','Choose the use meaning “cease to exist.”','The old custom vanished from the region.','The coin vanished behind the sofa.','The rabbit vanished into its burrow.','The custom no longer exists.')]);
P('vanished','Past participle of vanish; it describes something no longer visible or something that no longer exists.',[C('vanished.s1','看不见','The rescue team searched the vanished boat’s last known position in dense fog.','救援隊在濃霧中搜尋那艘失去蹤影的船最後出現的位置。','a vanished person / object','Adjective: no longer able to be seen after disappearing.','The boat is not visible where it was last reported.'),C('vanished.s2','已经灭绝','The museum displayed a model of a vanished species that has no living members today.','博物館展示了一種已滅絕物種的模型，如今已沒有存活個體。','a vanished species / language / custom','Adjective: no longer existing, often because it has died out.','No members of the species remain alive.')],[M('The vanished species has millions of living members today across every continent.','The widespread species has millions of living members today across every continent.','A species with living members has not vanished from existence.')],[Q('vanished.q1','vanished.s1','meaning','Why did rescuers search the boat’s last known position?','The boat could no longer be seen in the fog.','The boat was docked safely in daylight.','The species had become extinct.','The first sense means no longer visible.'),Q('vanished.q2','vanished.s2','context','What is true of the vanished species?','It has no living members today.','Millions of it live on every continent.','It is hidden in the fog but alive.','The species no longer exists.'),Q('vanished.q3','vanished.s1','distinction','Which item is vanished but may still exist?','A key lost from sight somewhere in the house.','A species that has died out.','A language with no speakers left.','The lost key is unseen but may still exist.'),Q('vanished.q4','vanished.s2','word-choice','Choose the use about extinction.','a vanished language with no speakers','a vanished boat behind a bank of fog','a vanished wallet misplaced at home','The language no longer exists as a living one.')]);
P('vanity','From Latin vanitas, “emptiness or worthlessness”; it means excessive pride or a show of pride without real value.',[C('vanity.s1','虚荣','Her vanity led her to reject any photograph that showed a wrinkle.','她的虛榮心使她拒絕任何拍到皺紋的照片。','vanity about + appearance / status','Noun: excessive pride in one’s appearance, ability, or achievement.','She is overly concerned with looking perfect.'),C('vanity.s2','虚有其表','The gold-plated trophy was a vanity, impressive to display but of no practical value.','這座鍍金獎盃只是虛有其表，展示起來醒目卻沒有實際價值。','an act / object of vanity','Noun: behaviour or an object showing excessive pride, or something with no real value.','The trophy is mainly a display of status.')],[M('Her vanity made her indifferent to praise or attention and unconcerned about her appearance.','Her humility made her indifferent to praise or attention and unconcerned about her appearance.','Indifference to one’s appearance and praise is not excessive self-pride.')],[Q('vanity.q1','vanity.s1','meaning','Why did she reject the photograph?','Her excessive pride made her dislike seeing a wrinkle.','She was proud of the natural photograph.','She wanted to help the photographer.','Vanity can mean excessive concern with appearance.'),Q('vanity.q2','vanity.s2','context','Why was the trophy called a vanity?','It was for display and had no practical value.','It was a useful tool for measuring water.','It was a valued colleague.','This sense can describe a showy object without real use.'),Q('vanity.q3','vanity.s1','distinction','Which behaviour shows vanity?','Someone demands praise for every minor achievement.','Someone is unconcerned with appearance or praise.','Someone checks a permit’s validity.','The first shows excessive pride.'),Q('vanity.q4','vanity.s2','word-choice','Choose the use about an empty display.','a gold-plated object bought only to flaunt status','a practical tool used daily in the workshop','a sincere compliment to a colleague','The object is a show of pride rather than useful value.')]);
P('vanquish','From Old French vencus, “conquered,” based on Latin vincere, “to conquer”; it means defeat or overcome.',[C('vanquish.s1','战胜敌人','The smaller army managed to vanquish the invading force at the mountain pass.','較小的軍隊設法在山口擊敗了入侵部隊。','vanquish an enemy / opponent','Transitive verb: defeat an enemy completely, especially in battle.','The invading force is beaten.'),C('vanquish.s2','克服困难','With steady practice, the singer vanquished her fear of performing before an audience.','透過持續練習，歌手克服了在觀眾面前表演的恐懼。','vanquish a fear / illness / obstacle','Transitive verb: overcome a feeling or illness through strong effort.','Practice helps her master the fear.')],[M('The army vanquished the enemy by surrendering and allowing it to take control of the pass.','The army was vanquished by the enemy after surrendering the pass.','Surrendering to the enemy is being vanquished, not defeating the enemy.')],[Q('vanquish.q1','vanquish.s1','meaning','What did the smaller army do?','Defeated the invading force at the pass.','Surrendered and let it take control.','Built a new railway.','Vanquish means defeat an enemy.'),Q('vanquish.q2','vanquish.s2','context','What did the singer vanquish?','Her fear of performing before an audience.','The audience itself.','A mountain pass in battle.','This sense means overcome a feeling.'),Q('vanquish.q3','vanquish.s1','distinction','Which action vanquishes an opponent?','Winning decisively against the rival force.','Letting the rival take the field.','Leaving the contest before it begins.','A decisive win defeats the opponent.'),Q('vanquish.q4','vanquish.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','He vanquished his fear of speaking in public.','The army vanquished its enemy in battle.','The general vanquished the invading force.','The first describes overcoming an emotion.')]);
P('vantage','From Old French avantage, “advantage,” with the initial syllable lost; it means a favorable viewpoint or a better chance.',[C('vantage.s1','有利位置','From the hilltop vantage, the surveyors could see the entire river bend.','測量員從山頂的有利位置看到了整個河灣。','a vantage point / position','Noun: a position that gives a good view or a better chance of success.','The hilltop allows a broad view.'),C('vantage.s2','胜算优势','The home team gained a vantage when its opponent lost two players to injury.','對手有兩名球員受傷離場後，主隊取得了勝算優勢。','gain / have a vantage over + opponent','Noun: a situation that gives someone a better chance of winning.','The team now has a competitive advantage.')],[M('The surveyors chose a vantage point in a deep valley that blocked their view of the river.','The surveyors chose a lookout point on the hill that gave them a clear view of the river.','A vantage point offers a good view, so the blocked valley is not one.')],[Q('vantage.q1','vantage.s1','meaning','Why was the hilltop a vantage?','It gave surveyors a clear view of the river bend.','It blocked every view of the river.','It made the team lose two players.','A vantage point provides a good view or position.'),Q('vantage.q2','vantage.s2','context','Why did the home team gain a vantage?','Its opponent lost two players and its chance of winning improved.','The team lost two players.','The match was cancelled before it began.','The situation gives the home team an advantage.'),Q('vantage.q3','vantage.s1','distinction','Which place offers a vantage point?','A tower overlooking the whole harbour.','A basement with no windows.','A valley hidden behind a ridge.','The tower provides a wide view.'),Q('vantage.q4','vantage.s2','word-choice','Choose the use about a better chance of success.','The early lead gave the team a vantage over its rivals.','The hilltop vantage revealed the river.','The observer chose a vantage point for the view.','The first describes a competitive advantage.')]);
P('vapor','From Latin vapor, “steam or exhalation”; it can mean gas formed from liquid or a visible mist of tiny droplets.',[C('vapor.s1','气态','Water vapor rose from the heated surface and spread through the sealed chamber.','水蒸氣從受熱表面升起，擴散到密封腔室中。','water / chemical vapor','Noun: gas that a liquid becomes when heated.','Heating changes liquid water into gaseous water vapor.'),C('vapor.s2','可见雾气','A pale vapor of tiny droplets formed above the kettle as the room cooled.','室內降溫時，水壺上方形成一團由微小水滴構成的淡白霧氣。','a visible vapor / cloud above + source','Noun: a visible mist made of tiny droplets in the air.','The white cloud is condensed droplets rather than invisible gas.')],[M('The vapor above the kettle was a dry solid block with no droplets or gas in the air.','The vapor above the kettle was a cloud of tiny water droplets.','Vapor in the visible-mist sense is a fine cloud of airborne droplets, not a solid.')],[Q('vapor.q1','vapor.s1','meaning','What happened to the water when heated?','It changed into gas and rose through the chamber.','It turned into a solid block.','It remained frozen.','Vapor can mean the gaseous state of a liquid.'),Q('vapor.q2','vapor.s2','context','What formed above the kettle as the room cooled?','A visible mist of tiny droplets.','A dry solid block.','An invisible metal pipe.','The second sense refers to a visible cloud of droplets.'),Q('vapor.q3','vapor.s1','distinction','Which example is water vapor in the gas sense?','Water molecules dispersed as gas after evaporation.','A visible cloud of condensed droplets.','A puddle still in liquid form.','The first is gaseous water.'),Q('vapor.q4','vapor.s2','word-choice','Which phrase uses the visible-mist sense?','a pale cloud of vapor drifting above the kettle','water vapor dispersed invisibly in the chamber','liquid water resting in a bowl','The cloud consists of tiny droplets visible in the air.')]);
P('vaporization','From vaporize + -ation; it names the phase change that turns a liquid or solid into gas.',[C('vaporization.s1','相变','Rapid vaporization turned the spilled solvent into gas when the laboratory heater was switched on.','實驗室加熱器開啟後，灑出的溶劑迅速汽化成氣體。','vaporization of + liquid / solid','Noun: the process of changing a liquid or solid into gas.','The solvent changes phase into gas.')],[M('The vaporization of the solvent turned the gas back into a solid without cooling or deposition.','The condensation of the solvent turned the gas back into liquid.','Vaporization produces gas from liquid or solid; gas turning to liquid is condensation.')],[Q('vaporization.q1','vaporization.s1','meaning','What happened to the spilled solvent?','It changed into gas when heated.','It froze into a solid.','It condensed from gas into liquid.','Vaporization is the phase change into gas.'),Q('vaporization.q2','vaporization.s1','context','Which process is vaporization?','Heating a liquid until it becomes gas.','Cooling a gas until droplets form.','Freezing water into ice.','The liquid-to-gas change is vaporization.'),Q('vaporization.q3','vaporization.s1','distinction','What can vaporization start from?','A liquid or a solid that changes into gas.','Only gas becoming liquid.','Only a solid melting into liquid.','The definition includes liquid or solid turning to gas.'),Q('vaporization.q4','vaporization.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct scientific phrase.','vaporization of the solvent into gas','vaporization of gas into liquid droplets','vaporization of ice into liquid water only','Vaporization means formation of gas from liquid or solid.')]);
P('vaporize','From vapor + -ize, ultimately from Latin vapor; it means change a substance into vapor or cause that change.',[C('vaporize.s1','变成气体','The alcohol will vaporize quickly if the open container is left near the warm radiator.','如果把敞口容器放在暖氣片附近，酒精會很快汽化。','a liquid vaporizes','Intransitive verb: change from liquid into vapor.','The alcohol changes to gas.'),C('vaporize.s2','使汽化','The technician used a heated coil to vaporize a small amount of the liquid sample.','技師用加熱線圈使少量液體樣本汽化。','vaporize + liquid / fuel','Transitive verb: make a liquid turn into vapor.','The coil causes the phase change.')],[M('The technician vaporized the liquid by freezing it into a block of ice.','The technician froze the liquid into a block of ice.','Freezing changes liquid to solid; it does not vaporize it.')],[Q('vaporize.q1','vaporize.s1','meaning','What will the alcohol do near the warm radiator?','Change from liquid into vapor.','Freeze into a block of ice.','Become a metal.','The intransitive sense describes a liquid changing to gas.'),Q('vaporize.q2','vaporize.s2','context','What did the heated coil do to the sample?','Caused some liquid to become vapor.','Cooled it until it froze.','Measured its price.','The transitive sense means make something vaporize.'),Q('vaporize.q3','vaporize.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses vaporize without an object?','The solvent vaporized in the warm room.','The heater vaporized the solvent.','The technician heated the solvent.','The first verb describes the liquid changing itself.'),Q('vaporize.q4','vaporize.s2','word-choice','Choose the transitive use.','Heat vaporized the fuel into gas.','The fuel vaporized after the cap was removed.','The gas condensed into drops.','The heat causes the fuel to change phase.')]);
P('variability','From variable + -ity, the quality of changing or the differences found among members of a group.',[C('variability.s1','易变程度','The variability of coastal winds makes the daily sailing schedule difficult to predict.','沿海風勢變化很大，讓每日航行時間難以預測。','variability in + weather / result','Noun: the tendency to change often or easily.','Wind conditions do not stay consistent.'),C('variability.s2','群体差异','The study measured variability in leaf size across trees growing at different elevations.','研究測量不同海拔樹木葉片大小的差異。','variability among / between + group members','Noun: differences between members of a group in biology or statistics.','Leaf sizes vary across the sampled trees.')],[M('The study reported variability in leaf size even though every tree had the same measured leaf dimensions.','The study reported no variability in leaf size because every tree had the same measured dimensions.','Identical measurements show no variation among the leaves.')],[Q('variability.q1','variability.s1','meaning','Why is the sailing schedule hard to predict?','Coastal winds change frequently.','The winds stay exactly the same every day.','The boats are never used.','Variability can mean a tendency to change.'),Q('variability.q2','variability.s2','context','What differences did the study measure?','Leaf sizes among trees at different elevations.','The price of a single boat.','The grammar of the word variable.','This sense is variation between group members.'),Q('variability.q3','variability.s1','distinction','Which condition has high variability?','Temperatures swing widely from hour to hour.','The temperature remains fixed at 20 degrees.','A clock displays the same time all day.','Frequent changes indicate variability.'),Q('variability.q4','variability.s2','word-choice','Choose the biological use.','variability in wing length among the sampled insects','variability of an unpredictable market price','variability in the wind forecast each day','The first compares measurements among members of a group.')]);
P('variable','From Latin variabilis, “changeable,” based on variare, “make different”; it describes something changeable or a quantity that can change.',[C('variable.s1','可变的','The variable wind speed forced the pilot to adjust the landing approach several times.','風速變化不定，迫使飛行員多次調整降落路線。','variable rate / amount / condition','Adjective: able to change or be changed, often in amount or speed.','The wind does not remain constant.'),C('variable.s2','数学或科学变量','In the equation, x is a variable whose value changes with the temperature.','在這個方程式中，x 是一個會隨溫度改變數值的變數。','a variable in + equation / experiment','Noun: a number, quantity, or factor that can change.','The symbol represents a changeable quantity.')],[M('The variable wind speed stayed exactly constant at the same value throughout every landing.','The constant wind speed stayed exactly the same throughout every landing.','A quantity that stays fixed is constant, not variable.')],[Q('variable.q1','variable.s1','meaning','Why did the pilot adjust the approach?','Wind speed changed and was not constant.','Wind speed stayed fixed for every landing.','The equation’s x changed with temperature.','The adjective variable means able to change.'),Q('variable.q2','variable.s2','context','What is x in the equation?','A quantity whose value can change with temperature.','A fixed word meaning valley.','A public electricity service.','A variable is a changeable number or factor.'),Q('variable.q3','variable.s1','distinction','Which weather is variable?','Wind shifts from calm to strong throughout the day.','Wind remains at the same speed all day.','A chart’s labels remain printed.','The wind changes in strength.'),Q('variable.q4','variable.s2','word-choice','Choose the mathematical use.','Let y be a variable in the equation.','The variable weather delayed the ferry.','The variable quality of the paint is inconsistent.','Here the noun names a quantity that can change.')]);
P('variance','From Latin variantia, “difference,” based on variare, “change”; it can mean difference or the statistical average squared distance from a mean.',[C('variance.s1','差异与统计','There was little variance in test scores, and the statistician calculated their variance from the mean.','測驗分數差異不大，統計學家並計算了它們相對平均值的變異數。','variance in / from + group or mean','Noun: the fact of being different; in statistics, the average squared distance from the mean.','The word covers general difference and a specific statistical measure.')],[M('The variance was zero even though the data points were widely spread around their mean.','The variance was high because the data points were widely spread around their mean.','Widely spread values have a high variance, not zero variance.')],[Q('variance.q1','variance.s1','meaning','What does variance describe generally?','The fact that values differ from one another.','The value that never changes.','A person leading a movement.','Variance can mean difference or variation.'),Q('variance.q2','variance.s1','context','What does the statistician calculate in the technical sense?','The average squared distance of scores from their mean.','The simple sum of all scores only.','The highest score without comparison.','Statistical variance uses squared distances from the mean.'),Q('variance.q3','variance.s1','distinction','Which data set has greater variance?','Scores spread widely around their average.','Scores clustered closely around their average.','A list containing one repeated score only.','Greater spread from the mean produces greater variance.'),Q('variance.q4','variance.s1','word-choice','Choose the statistical use.','The analyst compared variance across the two samples.','The analyst described the weather as variable.','The analyst measured the usefulness of a tool.','The statistic compares a measure of spread in the samples.')]);
})();

